{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Separates top-level balanced parenthesis groups from a string, ignoring spaces.\n    Assumes valid and balanced input due to critical constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    groups = []\n    balance = 0\n    start_index = 0\n\n    # Normalize: remove all whitespace characters\n    compacted_string = \"\".join(ch for ch in paren_string if not ch.isspace())\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(compacted_string):\n        if char == '(':\n            if balance == 0:\n                start_index = i  # Start of a new top-level group\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n            if balance == 0:\n                # End of a top-level balanced group\n                groups.append(compacted_string[start_index : i + 1])\n    return groups\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/0", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef has_close_elements(numbers: List[float], threshold: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" Check if in given list of numbers, any two numbers are closer to each other than\n    given threshold. The comparison is strict: abs(a - b) < threshold.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Sort the list to enable O(N log N) comparison of adjacent elements.\n    # Inputs are assumed to be valid per critical requirements.\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n    for i in range(1, len(sorted_numbers)):\n        if abs(sorted_numbers[i] - sorted_numbers[i-1]) < threshold:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/0", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef has_close_elements(numbers: List[float], threshold: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" Check if in given list of numbers, are any two numbers closer to each other than\n    given threshold.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n    for i in range(len(sorted_numbers) - 1):\n        if abs(sorted_numbers[i+1] - sorted_numbers[i]) < threshold:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string containing multiple groups of nested parentheses. Your goal is to\n    separate those group into separate strings and return the list of those.\n    Separate groups are balanced (each open brace is properly closed) and not nested within each other\n    Ignore any spaces in the input string.\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('( ) (( )) (( )( ))')\n    ['()', '(())', '(()())']\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_string = \"\".join(char for char in paren_string if not char.isspace())\n\n    depth = 0\n    start_index = None\n    groups: List[str] = []\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(normalized_string):\n        if char == '(':\n            if depth == 0:\n                start_index = i\n            depth += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            # Assuming valid inputs where depth will not go below zero and start_index is set.\n            depth -= 1\n            if depth == 0:\n                groups.append(normalized_string[start_index:i+1])\n    \n    return groups\n```"}
