{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "To implement the software design specification, I will generate the required files and their contents, adhering to the specified structure, classes, and methods. Per the critical requirements, unit tests will not be generated, and the final output format will consist solely of code blocks for each file.\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"gcd-service\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reliable library and small service to compute the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two integers.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.9,<4.0\"\nfastapi = { version = \"^0.109.0\", optional = true }\nuvicorn = { version = \"^0.27.0\", optional = true }\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\ngcd-service = \"gcd_service.__main__:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n[tool.poetry.extras]\napi = [\"fastapi\", \"uvicorn\"]\n```\n\n```text\n# requirements.txt\n# No mandatory runtime dependencies beyond built-in Python modules.\n# Optional API dependencies are managed via pyproject.toml extras.\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n\n# GCD Service\n\nA reliable library and small service to compute the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two integers,\nwith Python API, CLI, and an optional HTTP endpoint.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install the package using poetry:\n\n```bash\npoetry install\n```\n\nTo include the optional HTTP API dependencies:\n\n```bash\npoetry install --with api\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Python API\n\n```python\nfrom gcd_service import greatest_common_divisor\nfrom gcd_service.services import GCDService\nfrom gcd_service.config import Config\nfrom gcd_service.adapters.sqlite_adapter import SQLiteHistoryAdapter\nimport os\n\n# Compute GCD using the convenience function (no persistence)\nresult_value = greatest_common_divisor(25, 15)\nprint(f\"GCD(25, 15) = {result_value}\") # Output: 5\n\n# Example with persistence enabled\n# Ensure the data directory exists\nos.makedirs(\"./data\", exist_ok=True)\nconfig = Config(persistence_enabled=True, db_path=\"./data/my_gcd_history.db\")\nrepository = SQLiteHistoryAdapter(db_path=config.db_path)\nservice = GCDService(repository=repository, config=config)\n\nresult_dto = service.compute(30, 18)\nprint(f\"GCD({result_dto.a}, {result_dto.b}) = {result_dto.gcd} (computed at {result_dto.computed_at})\")\n\n# Retrieve history\nhistory = repository.list_recent(limit=5)\nfor record in history:\n    print(f\"History: a={record.a}, b={record.b}, gcd={record.gcd}, computed_at={record.computed_at.isoformat()}\")\n```\n\n### Command Line Interface (CLI)\n\n```bash\n# Compute GCD\ngcd-service compute --a 25 --b 15\n# Output: 5\n\n# Retrieve recent history (requires persistence enabled via env vars or config)\n# Example with persistence enabled via env var:\n# GCD_PERSISTENCE_ENABLED=true gcd-service history --limit 3\n# Output:\n# a=30, b=18, gcd=6, computed_at=2023-10-27T10:00:00.000000\n```\n\n### HTTP REST API (Optional)\n\nFirst, ensure you have the `api` extra installed:\n\n```bash\npoetry install --with api\n```\n\nTo start the API server:\n\n```bash\npython -m gcd_service.api\n```\n\nThe API will then be available, by default at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.\n\n-   **GET /gcd?a=<int>&b=<int>**\n    ```bash\n    curl \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/gcd?a=25&b=15\"\n    # Expected output: {\"a\":25,\"b\":15,\"gcd\":5,\"computed_at\":\"...\"}\n    ```\n-   **GET /history?limit=<int>**\n    ```bash\n    curl \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/history?limit=2\"\n    # Expected output: [{\"a\":...,\"b\":...,\"gcd\":...,\"computed_at\":\"...\"}, ...]\n    ```\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/__init__.py\nfrom .services import GCDService\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom .adapters.sqlite_adapter import SQLiteHistoryAdapter\n\ndef greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the greatest common divisor of two integers using the internal service.\n    This is a convenience wrapper for direct computation without history persistence.\n    \"\"\"\n    svc = GCDService(repository=None, config=Config(persistence_enabled=False))\n    return svc.compute(a, b).gcd\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"greatest_common_divisor\",\n    \"GCDService\",\n    \"Config\",\n    \"HistoryRepository\",\n    \"SQLiteHistoryAdapter\",\n]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/config.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"\n    Application configuration settings for persistence and error handling.\n    \"\"\"\n    persistence_enabled: bool = False\n    db_path: str = \"./data/gcd_history.db\"\n    fail_fast_on_db_error: bool = False\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/models.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\n@dataclass\nclass GCDResult:\n    \"\"\"\n    Data Transfer Object representing the result of a GCD computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    a: int\n    b: int\n    gcd: int\n    computed_at: datetime\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"\n        Converts the GCDResult object into a dictionary suitable for serialization.\n        \"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"a\": self.a,\n            \"b\": self.b,\n            \"gcd\": self.gcd,\n            \"computed_at\": self.computed_at.isoformat()\n        }\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/exceptions.py\nclass GCDInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised when inputs for GCD computation are invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass RepositoryError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised for failures during repository operations, wrapping underlying causes.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, cause: Exception | None = None) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.cause = cause\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/utils.py\nfrom .exceptions import GCDInputError\n\nclass GCDValidator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides static methods for validating and normalizing input values for GCD computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def ensure_int(value: object) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Attempts to convert a given value to an integer, raising GCDInputError on failure.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            return int(value)\n        except (ValueError, TypeError) as e:\n            raise GCDInputError(f\"Value '{value}' is not a valid integer.\") from e\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_and_normalize(a: object, b: object) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates that inputs `a` and `b` are integers and returns their absolute values.\n        \"\"\"\n        ai = GCDValidator.ensure_int(a)\n        bi = GCDValidator.ensure_int(b)\n        return abs(ai), abs(bi)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/services.py\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport logging\n\nfrom .models import GCDResult\nfrom .exceptions import RepositoryError\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom .config import Config\n\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass GCDService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates the core GCD computation logic and orchestrates history persistence.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repository: HistoryRepository | None, config: Config) -> None:\n        self._repo = repository\n        self._config = config\n\n    def compute(self, a: int, b: int) -> GCDResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the GCD of two integers, records the result if persistence is enabled,\n        and returns a GCDResult DTO.\n        \"\"\"\n        a_abs, b_abs = abs(a), abs(b) # Normalize inputs for the Euclidean algorithm\n\n        if a_abs == 0 and b_abs == 0:\n            result_gcd = 0\n        else:\n            result_gcd = self._euclidean_gcd(a_abs, b_abs)\n\n        res = GCDResult(a=a, b=b, gcd=result_gcd, computed_at=datetime.utcnow())\n\n        if self._config.persistence_enabled and self._repo:\n            try:\n                self._repo.insert(res)\n            except Exception as e:\n                if self._config.fail_fast_on_db_error:\n                    raise RepositoryError(\"DB insert failed\", e) from e\n                else:\n                    _logger.error(f\"Failed to persist GCD record (a={a}, b={b}, gcd={result_gcd}): {e}\", exc_info=True)\n        return res\n\n    def _euclidean_gcd(self, a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Internal method that implements the Euclidean algorithm for GCD.\n        Expects non-negative integers as inputs and returns a non-negative result.\n        \"\"\"\n        while b != 0:\n            a, b = b, a % b\n        return abs(a)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/repositories.py\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .models import GCDResult\n\nclass HistoryRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"\n    Abstract interface for managing GCD computation history persistence.\n    \"\"\"\n    @abstractmethod\n    def insert(self, record: GCDResult) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Inserts a GCDResult record into the history store.\n        Returns the unique ID of the newly inserted record.\n        \"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def list_recent(self, limit: int = 100) -> list[GCDResult]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieves a list of the most recent GCD computation records.\n        \"\"\"\n        pass\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/adapters/sqlite_adapter.py\nimport sqlite3\nimport os\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nfrom ..repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom ..models import GCDResult\nfrom ..exceptions import RepositoryError\n\nclass SQLiteHistoryAdapter(HistoryRepository):\n    \"\"\"\n    Concrete implementation of HistoryRepository using SQLite for storage.\n    Manages database schema and CRUD operations for history records.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str) -> None:\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._ensure_schema()\n\n    def _conn(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"\n        Establishes and returns a new SQLite database connection.\n        \"\"\"\n        return sqlite3.connect(self._db_path, detect_types=sqlite3.PARSE_DECLTYPES | sqlite3.PARSE_COLNAMES)\n\n    def _ensure_schema(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the SQLite database schema by creating the 'history' table if it doesn't exist,\n        along with necessary indexes.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            with self._conn() as conn:\n                conn.execute(\n                    \"\"\"\n                    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS history (\n                        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                        a INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                        b INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                        gcd INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                        computed_at TEXT NOT NULL\n                    )\n                    \"\"\"\n                )\n                conn.execute(\"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_history_computed_at ON history(computed_at DESC)\")\n                conn.commit()\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to ensure SQLite schema at {self._db_path}\", e) from e\n\n    def insert(self, record: GCDResult) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Inserts a GCDResult record into the SQLite history table.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            with self._conn() as conn:\n                cur = conn.execute(\n                    \"INSERT INTO history (a, b, gcd, computed_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                    (record.a, record.b, record.gcd, record.computed_at.isoformat()),\n                )\n                conn.commit()\n                return cur.lastrowid\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to insert history record into {self._db_path}\", e) from e\n\n    def list_recent(self, limit: int = 100) -> list[GCDResult]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieves a list of the most recent GCD computation records from the SQLite database.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            with self._conn() as conn:\n                cur = conn.execute(\n                    \"SELECT a, b, gcd, computed_at FROM history ORDER BY computed_at DESC LIMIT ?\",\n                    (limit,)\n                )\n                rows = cur.fetchall()\n                results = []\n                for r in rows:\n                    computed_at = datetime.fromisoformat(r[3])\n                    results.append(GCDResult(a=r[0], b=r[1], gcd=r[2], computed_at=computed_at))\n                return results\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to retrieve history records from {self._db_path}\", e) from e\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/controllers.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport logging\n\nfrom .utils import GCDValidator\nfrom .services import GCDService\nfrom .exceptions import GCDInputError, RepositoryError\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\n\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass GCDController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages the flow between presentation layers (CLI/API) and the core GCDService.\n    Handles input validation and converts service results to a suitable output format.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: GCDService) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n\n    def compute(self, a: object, b: object) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates raw inputs, calls GCDService to compute, and returns the result as a dictionary.\n        \"\"\"\n        a_norm, b_norm = GCDValidator.validate_and_normalize(a, b)\n        result = self._service.compute(a_norm, b_norm)\n        return result.to_dict()\n\n    def history(self, limit: int = 100) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieves recent GCD computation history records via the configured repository.\n        Returns an empty list if persistence is disabled or retrieval fails gracefully.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self._service._repo and self._service._config.persistence_enabled:\n            try:\n                records = self._service._repo.list_recent(limit)\n                return [record.to_dict() for record in records]\n            except RepositoryError as e:\n                _logger.error(f\"Could not retrieve history records: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n                return []\n        return []\n\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles command-line argument parsing, delegates to GCDController,\n    and manages CLI-specific output and error reporting.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, controller: GCDController) -> None:\n        self._controller = controller\n\n    def run(self, argv: list[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses command-line arguments and executes the corresponding GCD operation.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for errors).\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"gcd-service\",\n            description=\"Compute GCD of two integers or manage history.\",\n            formatter_class=argparse.RawTextHelpFormatter\n        )\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", help=\"Available commands\")\n\n        compute_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"compute\", help=\"Compute the GCD of two integers.\")\n        compute_parser.add_argument(\"--a\", type=str, required=True, help=\"First integer.\")\n        compute_parser.add_argument(\"--b\", type=str, required=True, help=\"Second integer.\")\n\n        history_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"history\", help=\"Retrieve recent GCD computation history.\")\n        history_parser.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=10, help=\"Number of recent records to retrieve (default: 10).\")\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        if args.command == \"compute\":\n            try:\n                out = self._controller.compute(args.a, args.b)\n                print(out[\"gcd\"])\n                return 0\n            except GCDInputError as e:\n                print(f\"Error: Invalid input: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 2\n            except Exception as e:\n                _logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred during CLI compute.\")\n                print(f\"Error: An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n\n        elif args.command == \"history\":\n            try:\n                history_records = self._controller.history(args.limit)\n                if not history_records:\n                    print(\"No history records found or persistence is disabled.\", file=sys.stderr)\n                else:\n                    for record in history_records:\n                        print(f\"a={record['a']}, b={record['b']}, gcd={record['gcd']}, computed_at={record['computed_at']}\")\n                return 0\n            except Exception as e:\n                _logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred during CLI history retrieval.\")\n                print(f\"Error: An unexpected error occurred while retrieving history: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n        else:\n            parser.print_help(sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/api.py\nimport uvicorn\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Query\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\nfrom typing import List\nimport logging\nimport os\n\nfrom .controllers import GCDController\nfrom .exceptions import GCDInputError\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .services import GCDService\nfrom .adapters.sqlite_adapter import SQLiteHistoryAdapter\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\n\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass APIServer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages the FastAPI application, its endpoints, and lifecycle for the GCD service.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, controller: GCDController) -> None:\n        self._controller = controller\n        self.app = self._create_app()\n\n    def _create_app(self) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes and configures the FastAPI application with API endpoints.\n        \"\"\"\n        app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"GCD Service API\",\n            description=\"API for computing Greatest Common Divisor and viewing history.\",\n            version=\"0.1.0\"\n        )\n\n        @app.get(\"/gcd\", response_model=dict, summary=\"Compute GCD of two integers\")\n        async def get_gcd_endpoint(\n            a: str = Query(..., description=\"First integer\"),\n            b: str = Query(..., description=\"Second integer\")\n        ) -> JSONResponse:\n            \"\"\"\n            Computes the greatest common divisor of `a` and `b`.\n            \"\"\"\n            try:\n                result = self._controller.compute(a, b)\n                return JSONResponse(content=result)\n            except GCDInputError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e))\n            except Exception as e:\n                _logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred during GCD computation via API.\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Internal Server Error\")\n\n        @app.get(\"/history\", response_model=List[dict], summary=\"Get computation history\")\n        async def get_history_endpoint(\n            limit: int = Query(100, ge=1, description=\"Number of recent records to retrieve\")\n        ) -> JSONResponse:\n            \"\"\"\n            Retrieves recent GCD computation history records, limited by `limit`.\n            \"\"\"\n            try:\n                history_records = self._controller.history(limit)\n                return JSONResponse(content=history_records)\n            except Exception as e:\n                _logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred during history retrieval via API.\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Internal Server Error\")\n\n        return app\n\n    def start(self, host: str = \"127.0.0.1\", port: int = 8000) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Starts the Uvicorn server to host the FastAPI application.\n        \"\"\"\n        _logger.info(f\"Starting API server at http://{host}:{port}\")\n        uvicorn.run(self.app, host=host, port=port)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\n    cfg = Config(\n        persistence_enabled=os.getenv(\"GCD_PERSISTENCE_ENABLED\", \"False\").lower() == \"true\",\n        db_path=os.getenv(\"GCD_DB_PATH\", \"./data/gcd_history.db\"),\n        fail_fast_on_db_error=os.getenv(\"GCD_FAIL_FAST_ON_DB_ERROR\", \"False\").lower() == \"true\"\n    )\n\n    repository: HistoryRepository | None = None\n    if cfg.persistence_enabled:\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(cfg.db_path), exist_ok=True)\n        repository = SQLiteHistoryAdapter(db_path=cfg.db_path)\n        _logger.info(f\"Persistence enabled. Using SQLite database at: {cfg.db_path}\")\n    else:\n        _logger.info(\"Persistence is disabled.\")\n\n    service = GCDService(repository=repository, config=cfg)\n    controller = GCDController(service)\n    api_server = APIServer(controller)\n\n    api_host = os.getenv(\"GCD_API_HOST\", \"127.0.0.1\")\n    api_port = int(os.getenv(\"GCD_API_PORT\", \"8000\"))\n\n    api_server.start(host=api_host, port=api_port)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/cli.py\nimport sys\n\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\n\nclass CLIApp:\n    \"\"\"\n    The main command-line interface application that orchestrates CLI functionality.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, controller: CLIController) -> None:\n        self._controller = controller\n\n    def run(self, argv: list[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Executes the CLI command based on provided arguments.\n        Delegates command parsing and execution to the CLIController.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self._controller.run(argv)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/gcd_service/__main__.py\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport logging\n\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .services import GCDService\nfrom .controllers import GCDController, CLIController\nfrom .cli import CLIApp\nfrom .adapters.sqlite_adapter import SQLiteHistoryAdapter\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\n\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    The main entry point for the `python -m gcd_service` command.\n    Initializes application components and runs the CLI.\n    \"\"\"\n    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\n    cfg = Config(\n        persistence_enabled=os.getenv(\"GCD_PERSISTENCE_ENABLED\", \"False\").lower() == \"true\",\n        db_path=os.getenv(\"GCD_DB_PATH\", \"./data/gcd_history.db\"),\n        fail_fast_on_db_error=os.getenv(\"GCD_FAIL_FAST_ON_DB_ERROR\", \"False\").lower() == \"true\"\n    )\n\n    repository: HistoryRepository | None = None\n    if cfg.persistence_enabled:\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(cfg.db_path), exist_ok=True)\n        repository = SQLiteHistoryAdapter(db_path=cfg.db_path)\n        _logger.info(f\"Persistence enabled. Using SQLite database at: {cfg.db_path}\")\n    else:\n        _logger.info(\"Persistence is disabled.\")\n\n    service = GCDService(repository=repository, config=cfg)\n    gcd_controller = GCDController(service)\n    cli_controller = CLIController(gcd_controller)\n    app = CLIApp(cli_controller)\n    sys.exit(app.run(argv or sys.argv[1:]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```"}
