{"task_id": "HumanEval/22", "solution": "```\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"intfilter\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python library to filter lists for integer values.\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"you@example.com\" }]\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nreadme = \"README.md\"\n\ndependencies = [\n    \"fastapi>=0.111.0\",\n    \"uvicorn[standard]>=0.30.1\",\n]\n\n[project.scripts]\nintfilter = \"scripts.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\", \"wheel\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\"src\"]\n\n[tool.setuptools.package-data]\n\"intfilter\" = [\"py.typed\"]\n\n```\n# README.md\n# intfilter\n\nA Python library, CLI, and HTTP API for filtering lists to extract only integer values.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install intfilter\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom intfilter import filter_integers, FilterService, TypeValidator, FileRepository\nimport logging\n\n# Direct function\nvalues = [1, 'a', 2.5, True, 3, False, '4', None]\nresult = filter_integers(values)\nprint(f\"Direct function result: {result}\") # Expected: [1, 3]\n\n# Using the service with optional persistence\nvalidator = TypeValidator()\nrepository = FileRepository() # Defaults to ~/.intfilter/history.log\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"intfilter_example\")\nlogger.setLevel(logging.INFO)\nhandler = logging.StreamHandler()\nformatter = logging.Formatter('%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\nhandler.setFormatter(formatter)\nlogger.addHandler(handler)\n\nservice = FilterService(validator=validator, repository=repository, persist=True, logger=logger)\nresult_with_persist = service.filter([10, \"foo\", 20, False])\nprint(f\"Service filter result with persistence: {result_with_persist}\") # Expected: [10, 20]\n# Check ~/.intfilter/history.log for audit record.\n```\n\n### Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\n```bash\n# Filter values provided directly\nintfilter --values '[1, \"hello\", 2, 3.14, True, 4]'\n# Expected: [1, 2, 4]\n\n# Filter values from a JSON file\necho '[5, \"world\", 6, False, 7]' > input.json\nintfilter --file input.json\n# Expected: [5, 6, 7]\n\n# With persistence enabled\nintfilter --values '[8, \"test\", 9]' --persist\n# An audit record will be written to ~/.intfilter/history.log\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nTo run the HTTP API:\n\n```bash\nuvicorn intfilter.api:get_app --factory --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThen, you can make requests:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8000/filter -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"values\": [1, \"a\", 2.0, 3, True, 4]}'\n# Expected: {\"result\":[1,3,4]}\n```\n```\n# LICENSE\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2024 Your Name\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n```\n# src/intfilter/__init__.py\nfrom typing import List, Any\nimport logging\n\nfrom .services import FilterService\nfrom .validators import TypeValidator\nfrom .repository import FileRepository\nfrom .api import APIController\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef filter_integers(values: List[Any]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Filters a list, returning only strict Python integers. Booleans are excluded.\"\"\"\n    validator = TypeValidator()\n    if values is None:\n        values_to_process = []\n    else:\n        values_to_process = list(values)\n\n    if not validator.is_valid_iterable(values_to_process):\n        raise ValidationError(\"Input 'values' must be an iterable (e.g., list, tuple), not str or bytes.\")\n        \n    return validator.filter_integers(values_to_process)\n\n__all__ = [\"filter_integers\", \"FilterService\", \"FileRepository\", \"TypeValidator\", \"ValidationError\", \"PersistenceError\"]\n\ndef get_app():\n    \"\"\"Returns the configured FastAPI application instance.\"\"\"\n    validator = TypeValidator()\n    repository = FileRepository()\n    service = FilterService(validator=validator, repository=repository, persist=True, logger=_logger)\n    api_controller = APIController(service=service)\n    return api_controller.get_app()\n\n```\n# src/intfilter/models.py\nfrom typing import Any, List, Dict\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nclass FilterResult:\n    \"\"\"Represents an audit record of a filtering operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, timestamp: str, input_values: List[Any], result_values: List[int]) -> None:\n        self.timestamp = timestamp\n        self.input_values = input_values\n        self.result_values = result_values\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Serializes the FilterResult object to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"timestamp\": self.timestamp,\n            \"input\": self.input_values,\n            \"result\": self.result_values\n        }\n\nDEFAULT_TIMESTAMP_FORMAT = \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z\"\n\n```\n# src/intfilter/services.py\nfrom typing import List, Optional, Any\nimport logging\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nfrom .validators import TypeValidator\nfrom .repository import FileRepository\nfrom .models import FilterResult\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\n\nclass FilterService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates filtering, logging, and optional persistence of filter operations.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_PERSIST = False\n\n    def __init__(self, validator: TypeValidator, repository: Optional[FileRepository]=None, persist: bool=DEFAULT_PERSIST, logger: Optional[logging.Logger]=None) -> None:\n        self.validator = validator\n        self.repository = repository\n        self.persist = persist\n        self.logger = logger or logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n    def _build_record(self, input_values: List[Any], result_values: List[int]) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Creates a dictionary representing an audit record for persistence.\"\"\"\n        # Use UTC timestamp with 'Z' suffix for clarity\n        timestamp = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='seconds').replace('+00:00', 'Z')\n        filter_result = FilterResult(timestamp=timestamp, input_values=input_values, result_values=result_values)\n        return filter_result.to_dict()\n\n    def filter(self, values: Optional[List[Any]]) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Validates input, filters for integers, and optionally persists the operation.\"\"\"\n        if values is None:\n            values_to_process = []\n        else:\n            values_to_process = list(values)\n\n        if not self.validator.is_valid_iterable(values_to_process):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input 'values' must be an iterable (e.g., list, tuple), not str or bytes.\")\n        \n        filtered_result = self.validator.filter_integers(values_to_process)\n        \n        if self.persist and self.repository:\n            record = self._build_record(values_to_process, filtered_result)\n            try:\n                self.repository.save(record)\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                self.logger.error(\"Persistence failed: %s\", e)\n                raise\n            except Exception as e:\n                self.logger.critical(\"Unexpected error during persistence: %s\", e, exc_info=True)\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"Unexpected error during persistence: {e}\") from e\n                \n        return filtered_result\n\n```\n# src/intfilter/validators.py\nfrom typing import Any, List\nfrom .utils import is_iterable\n\nclass TypeValidator:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates domain rules for identifying valid integer types and iterables.\"\"\"\n    def is_valid_iterable(self, values: Any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Returns True if values is iterable (excluding str and bytes).\"\"\"\n        return is_iterable(values)\n\n    def is_integer(self, value: Any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Returns True if the value is a strict Python int, excluding booleans.\"\"\"\n        return type(value) is int and not isinstance(value, bool)\n\n    def filter_integers(self, values: List[Any]) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Filters a list to return only strict Python integers, preserving order.\"\"\"\n        return [v for v in values if self.is_integer(v)]\n\n```\n# src/intfilter/repository.py\nimport json, os\nimport threading\nfrom typing import Dict\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\n\nclass FileRepository:\n    \"\"\"Handles persistence of audit records to a newline-delimited JSON file.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_HISTORY_PATH = \"~/.intfilter/history.log\"\n\n    def __init__(self, path: str = DEFAULT_HISTORY_PATH) -> None:\n        self.path = os.path.expanduser(path)\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self.path), exist_ok=True)\n        self._lock = threading.Lock()\n\n    def save(self, record: Dict) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a JSON record as a new line to the persistence file.\"\"\"\n        with self._lock:\n            try:\n       