dular design to easily add more filtering logic.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install prefix-filter\n```\n\nTo install with API support:\n\n```bash\npip install \"prefix-filter[api]\"\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom prefix_filter import filter_by_prefix\n\nstrings = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"apricot\", \"grape\"]\nprefix = \"ap\"\n\nfiltered_strings = filter_by_prefix(strings, prefix)\nprint(filtered_strings)\n# Expected output: ['apple', 'apricot']\n\n# Empty prefix matches all\nall_strings = filter_by_prefix(strings, \"\")\nprint(all_strings)\n# Expected output: ['apple', 'banana', 'apricot', 'grape']\n```\n\n### Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nFilter strings directly:\n\n```bash\nprefix-filter --prefix ap apple banana apricot grape\n# Expected output:\n# apple\n# apricot\n```\n\nFilter from an input file and save to an output file:\n\n`input.txt`:\n```\napple\nbanana\napricot\ngrape\n```\n\n```bash\nprefix-filter --prefix ap --input-file input.txt --output-file output.txt\n```\n\n`output.txt` will contain:\n```\napple\napricot\n```\n\n### REST API (Optional)\n\nFirst, ensure you have installed with API support: `pip install \"prefix-filter[api]\"`.\n\nRun the API server:\n\n```bash\nuvicorn prefix_filter.api:create_app --factory --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThen, send a POST request:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/filter\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{ \"strings\": [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"apricot\", \"grape\"], \"prefix\": \"ap\" }'\n```\n\nExpected JSON response:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"results\": [\n    \"apple\",\n    \"apricot\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Development\n\nClone the repository:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/prefix-filter.git\ncd prefix-filter\n```\n\nInstall development dependencies:\n\n```bash\npip install -e \".[api]\" # -e for editable mode, [api] for API dependencies\n```\n\nRun tests:\n\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License - see the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details.\n```\n\n```markdown\n# LICENSE\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2024 Your Name\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n```\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: Python CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n    paths:\n      - 'src/**'\n      - 'tests/**'\n      - 'pyproject.toml'\n      - '.github/workflows/ci.yml'\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n    paths:\n      - 'src/**'\n      - 'tests/**'\n      - 'pyproject.toml'\n      - '.github/workflows/ci.yml'\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.10\", \"3.11\", \"3.12\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        python -m pip install --upgrade pip\n        pip install -e \".[api]\" # Install editable with optional API dependencies for full test coverage\n        pip install pytest # pytest for running tests\n\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: |\n        pytest\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/__init__.py\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .services import PrefixFilterService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n__all__ = [\"filter_by_prefix\", \"InvalidInputError\"]\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\ndef filter_by_prefix(strings: List[str], prefix: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of strings, returning only those that start with the specified prefix.\n    This is a convenience wrapper that uses the core PrefixFilterService.\n    \"\"\"\n    svc = PrefixFilterService()\n    return svc.filter(strings, prefix)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/models.py\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass FilterRequest:\n    \"\"\"DTO for filtering requests.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, strings: List[str], prefix: str) -> None:\n        self.strings = strings\n        self.prefix = prefix\n\nclass FilterResult:\n    \"\"\"DTO for filtering results.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, results: List[str]) -> None:\n        self.results = results\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/services.py\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .utils import validate_strings, validate_prefix\nfrom .repositories import InMemoryStringRepository\n\nclass PrefixFilterService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Core business logic for prefix filtering.\n    It performs validation, filtering, and optionally uses a repository.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repo: Optional[InMemoryStringRepository] = None) -> None:\n        self.repo = repo\n\n    def filter(self, strings: List[str], prefix: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Filters a list of strings, returning only those that start with the specified prefix.\n        Performs input validation and preserves original order.\n        \"\"\"\n        validate_strings(strings)\n        validate_prefix(prefix)\n\n        if prefix == \"\":\n            return list(strings)  # Return a shallow copy if prefix is empty\n\n        results = [s for s in strings if self._matches(s, prefix)]\n\n        if self.repo:\n            self.repo.store(strings)  # Optionally store input strings\n\n        return results\n\n    def _matches(self, s: str, prefix: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Helper method to check if a string starts with a prefix.\"\"\"\n        return s.startswith(prefix)\n\n# Convenience module-level function, also used by __init__.py\ndef filter_by_prefix(strings: List[str], prefix: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters an input list of strings, returning only those that start with the given prefix.\n    This function leverages the PrefixFilterService for its functionality.\n    \"\"\"\n    svc = PrefixFilterService()\n    return svc.filter(strings, prefix)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/repositories.py\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass InMemoryStringRepository:\n    \"\"\"\n    An in-memory repository for storing lists of strings.\n    Primarily for demonstration or simple caching/auditing within the service.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._store: List[str] = []\n\n    def store(self, strings: List[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stores a copy of the given list of strings.\"\"\"\n        self._store = list(strings)\n\n    def read_list(self) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a shallow copy of the currently stored list of strings.\"\"\"\n        return list(self._store)\n\n    def clear(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Clears the stored list of strings.\"\"\"\n        self._store = []\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/controllers.py\nfrom .services import PrefixFilterService\nfrom .models import FilterRequest, FilterResult\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass PrefixFilterController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Mediates between external interfaces (CLI/API) and the core service.\n    It adapts requests and handles service responses and exceptions.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: PrefixFilterService) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n\n    def filter(self, request: FilterRequest) -> FilterResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Processes a FilterRequest, delegates to the service, and returns a FilterResult.\n        Propagates InvalidInputError for adapters to handle.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Basic validation of request DTO types (already validated by services.filter, but good practice here too)\n        if not isinstance(request, FilterRequest):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Request must be an instance of FilterRequest.\")\n\n        # Service.filter will perform detailed validation and raise InvalidInputError\n        results = self._service.filter(request.strings, request.prefix)\n        return FilterResult(results)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/exceptions.py\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"\n    Custom exception raised for invalid input data.\n    This provides a domain-specific error type for validation failures.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/utils.py\nfrom typing import Any, Iterable\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef validate_strings(strings: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates that 'strings' is a list or tuple containing only string elements.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if validation fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    if strings is None:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"strings must be provided and cannot be None\")\n    if not isinstance(strings, (list, tuple)):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"strings must be a list or tuple of str\")\n    for i, s in enumerate(strings):\n        if not isinstance(s, str):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"element at index {i} is not a str\")\n\ndef validate_prefix(prefix: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates that 'prefix' is a string.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if validation fails. An empty string is allowed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(prefix, str):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"prefix must be a str\")\n    # Empty prefix is explicitly allowed by business rules\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/cli.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, TextIO, Optional\n\nfrom .services import PrefixFilterService\nfrom .controllers import PrefixFilterController\nfrom .models import FilterRequest\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass CLIApp:\n    \"\"\"\n    Command-line interface application for prefix filtering.\n    Handles argument parsing, file I/O, and interacts with the controller.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, controller: PrefixFilterController) -> None:\n        self._controller = controller\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses command-line arguments, executes the filtering logic,\n        and prints results or writes to a file.\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = self._setup_arg_parser()\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n\n        try:\n            strings_to_filter: List[str] = []\n            if args.input_file:\n                with open(args.input_file, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                    strings_to_filter = [line.strip() for line in f if line.strip()]\n            elif args.strings:\n                strings_to_filter = args.strings\n            else:\n                parser.error(\"No input strings provided. Use positional arguments or --input-file.\")\n\n            request = FilterRequest(strings=strings_to_filter, prefix=args.prefix)\n            result = self._controller.filter(request)\n\n            if args.output_file:\n                with open(args.output_file, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                    for s in result.results:\n                        f.write(s + '\\n')\n            else:\n                for s in result.results:\n                    print(s)\n            return 0  # Success\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: Invalid input: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2  # Invalid usage/input\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            print(f\"Error: Input file '{args.input_file}' not found.\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Runtime error\n\n    def _setup_arg_parser(self) -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n        \"\"\"Configures and returns the argument parser for the CLI.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Filter a list of strings by a specified prefix.\",\n            formatter_class=argparse.RawTextHelpFormatter\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            '--prefix',\n            type=str,\n            required=True,\n            help=\"The prefix to filter strings by.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            '--input-file',\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Path to a newline-delimited file containing strings to filter.\"\n                 \"\\nCannot be used with positional STRING arguments.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            '--output-file',\n            type=str,\n            help=\"Path to a file where filtered results will be written (newline-delimited).\"\n                 \"\\nIf not specified, results are printed to stdout.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            'strings',\n            nargs='*', # 0 or more positional arguments\n            help=\"Space-separated strings to filter. Cannot be used with --input-file.\"\n        )\n\n        # Custom logic for mutual exclusivity of strings and input_file\n        def check_args(args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\n            if args.input_file and args.strings:\n                parser.error(\"argument --input-file cannot be used with positional STRING arguments.\")\n        parser.parse_args = lambda args=sys.argv[1:], namespace=None: (  # type: ignore\n            _args := argparse.ArgumentParser.parse_args(parser, args, namespace),\n            check_args(_args),\n            _args\n        )[2] # Wrapper to execute custom check immediately after parsing\n\n        return parser\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n    service = PrefixFilterService()\n    controller = PrefixFilterController(service)\n    app = CLIApp(controller)\n    return app.run(sys.argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n```python\n# src/prefix_filter/api.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nfrom .services import PrefixFilterService\nfrom .controllers import PrefixFilterController\nfrom .models import FilterRequest, FilterResult\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n# Pydantic models for API request/response validation\nclass ApiFilterRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Pydantic model for the incoming API request payload.\"\"\"\n    strings: List[str]\n    prefix: str\n\nclass ApiFilterResult(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Pydantic model for the outgoing API response payload.\"\"\"\n    results: List[str]\n\nclass FastAPIAdapter:\n    \"\"\"\n    Adapter class to integrate the prefix filtering functionality with FastAPI.\n    It encapsulates the FastAPI application creation and routing.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: PrefixFilterService) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n        self._controller = PrefixFilterController(service)\n\n    def create_app(self) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"\n        Creates and configures a FastAPI application with the /filter endpoint.\n        Converts API specific models to internal DTOs and handles exceptions.\n        \"\"\"\n        app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"Prefix Filter API\",\n            description=\"API for filtering lists of strings by a prefix.\",\n            version=__import__('prefix_filter').__version__\n        )\n\n        @app.post(\"/filter\", response_model=ApiFilterResult, status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK)\n        async def filter_strings(request_payload: ApiFilterRequest):\n            \"\"\"\n            Filters a list of strings by the specified prefix.\n            Expects a JSON payload with \"strings\" (List[str]) and \"prefix\" (str).\n            \"\"\"\n            try:\n                # Convert Pydantic model to internal DTO\n                internal_request = FilterRequest(\n                    strings=request_payload.strings,\n                    prefix=request_payload.prefix\n                )\n                internal_result = self._controller.filter(internal_request)\n                # Convert internal DTO back to Pydantic model for response\n                return ApiFilterResult(results=internal_result.results)\n            except InvalidInputError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST,\n                    detail={\"error\": e.message}\n                )\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Catch any unexpected errors\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR,\n                    detail={\"error\": f\"An unexpected error occurred: {str(e)}\"}\n                )\n        return app\n\ndef create_app() -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"Factory function to create the FastAPI application instance.\"\"\"\n    service = PrefixFilterService()\n    adapter = FastAPIAdapter(service)\n    return adapter.create_app()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import uvicorn\n    # Example usage for local development\n    app = create_app()\n    uvicorn.run(app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000)\n```"}
