e.\n- **CLI**: Run `fizzbuzz count --n <value>` to quickly get counts.\n- **HTTP API**: Access the functionality via `GET /count?n=<value>` endpoint.\n- **Modular Design**: Built with testability and maintainability in mind.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/fizzbuzz.git\ncd fizzbuzz\npip install poetry # If not already installed\npoetry install\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom fizzbuzz import count_sevens\n\n# Example: count '7's in numbers less than 79, divisible by 11 or 13\nresult = count_sevens(79)\nprint(f\"Count for n=79: {result}\") # Output: Count for n=79: 3\n```\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\npoetry run fizzbuzz count --n 79\n# Output: 3\n\npoetry run fizzbuzz count --n 50\n# Output: 0\n\npoetry run fizzbuzz count --n -1\n# Output: Error: Parameter 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nTo run the HTTP service:\n\n```bash\npoetry run uvicorn fizzbuzz.api:APIController.app --factory --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThen access the endpoint:\n\n```bash\ncurl \"http://localhost:8000/count?n=79\"\n# Output: {\"n\":79,\"count\":3}\n\ncurl \"http://localhost:8000/count?n=78\"\n# Output: {\"n\":78,\"count\":2}\n\ncurl \"http://localhost:8000/count?n=-1\"\n# Output: {\"detail\":\"Parameter 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\"}\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\n### Docker\n\nA Dockerfile is provided for containerization.\n\n```bash\ndocker build -t fizzbuzz-app .\ndocker run -p 8000:8000 fizzbuzz-app\n```\n\nThen you can access the API at `http://localhost:8000/count?n=...`.\n\n```\n\n```\n\nDockerfile\n```dockerfile\n# Use an official Python runtime as a parent image\nFROM python:3.9-slim-buster\n\n# Set the working directory in the container\nWORKDIR /app\n\n# Install system dependencies needed for Python packages\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n    build-essential \\\n    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n\n# Copy pyproject.toml and poetry.lock (if using poetry) or requirements.txt first\n# to leverage Docker cache\nCOPY pyproject.toml ./\nCOPY requirements.txt ./\n\n# Install poetry if not already present\nRUN pip install poetry\n\n# Install dependencies using poetry\nRUN poetry config virtualenvs.create false \\\n    && poetry install --no-root --no-dev --sync\n\n# Copy the rest of your application code\nCOPY src/ fizzbuzz/\n\n# Expose the port the app runs on\nEXPOSE 8000\n\n# Command to run the application\n# Use --factory to load the app from the APIController class\nCMD [\"uvicorn\", \"fizzbuzz.api:APIController.app\", \"--factory\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8000\"]\n\n```\n\n.github/workflows/ci.yml\n```yaml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n\njobs:\n  build-and-test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: '3.9' # Or appropriate version from pyproject.toml\n\n    - name: Install Poetry\n      run: pip install poetry\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: poetry install --no-root\n\n    - name: Run Linting (Ruff)\n      run: poetry run ruff check src/ tests/\n\n    - name: Run Type Checking (Mypy)\n      run: poetry run mypy src/\n\n    - name: Run Tests\n      run: poetry run pytest\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/36", "solution": "def fizz_buzz(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the number of times the digit 7 appears in integers less than n which are divisible by 11 or 13.\n    >>> fizz_buzz(50)\n    0\n    >>> fizz_buzz(78)\n    2\n    >>> fizz_buzz(79)\n    3\n    \"\"\"\n    candidates = set()\n\n    # Generate unique multiples of 11 less than n.\n    k = 0\n    while k < n:\n        candidates.add(k)\n        k += 11\n\n    # Generate unique multiples of 13 less than n.\n    k = 0\n    while k < n:\n        candidates.add(k)\n        k += 13\n\n    total_sevens_count = 0\n    for num in candidates:\n        total_sevens_count += str(num).count('7')\n\n    return total_sevens_count"}
