{"task_id": "HumanEval/41", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n# This file defines the project metadata and dependencies.\n# It should be placed in the project root.\n\n# [project]\n# name = \"car-collision-app\"\n# version = \"0.1.0\"\n# description = \"A Python library for computing car collisions with CLI and optional HTTP API.\"\n# authors = [\n#     { name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" },\n# ]\n# dependencies = [\n#     # No heavy dependencies for core lib\n# ]\n# requires-python = \">=3.9\"\n# readme = \"README.md\"\n# license = { text = \"MIT\" }\n# keywords = [\"collisions\", \"cars\", \"simulation\", \"cli\", \"api\"]\n# classifiers = [\n#     \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n#     \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n#     \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n# ]\n#\n# [project.optional-dependencies]\n# api = [\"fastapi>=0.100.0\", \"uvicorn>=0.22.0\"]\n# dev = [\"pytest>=7.0\", \"fastapi>=0.100.0\", \"uvicorn>=0.22.0\"]\n#\n# [project.scripts]\n# car-collision = \"car_collision_app.main:main\"\n#\n# [build-system]\n# requires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\n# build-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n```\n\n```python\n# README.md\n# This file provides an overview, installation, and usage instructions.\n# It should be placed in the project root.\n\n# # Car Collision App\n#\n# A Python library for computing the number of collisions between two groups of cars moving in opposite directions. It provides a programmatic interface, a command-line interface (CLI), and an optional HTTP API.\n#\n# ## Features\n# - Core collision calculation (`n * n`).\n# - Input validation with meaningful error messages.\n# - Command-Line Interface.\n# - Optional HTTP API for remote integration.\n#\n# ## Installation\n#\n# 1. **Clone the repository:**\n#    ```bash\n#    git clone https://github.com/yourusername/car-collision-app.git\n#    cd car-collision-app\n#    ```\n#\n# 2. **Install with Poetry (recommended):**\n#    ```bash\n#    poetry install\n#    # For API functionality:\n#    poetry install -E api\n#    ```\n#\n#    Or with `pip`:\n#    ```bash\n#    pip install .\n#    # For API functionality:\n#    pip install \".[api]\"\n#    ```\n#\n# ## Usage\n#\n# ### 1. Library (Python)\n#\n# You can import and use the `CollisionService` directly in your Python code:\n#\n# ```python\n# from car_collision_app.services.collision_service import CollisionService\n#\n# svc = CollisionService()\n# num_cars = 5\n# collisions = svc.collision_count(num_cars)\n# print(f\"For {num_cars} cars per side, there are {collisions} collisions.\")\n# # Output: For 5 cars per side, there are 25 collisions.\n# ```\n#\n# ### 2. Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n#\n# After installation, a `car-collision` command will be available:\n#\n# ```bash\n# car-collision 10\n# # Output: 100\n# ```\n#\n# Invalid input will result in an error message:\n#\n# ```bash\n# car-collision -5\n# # Output: n must be a non-negative integer\n# ```\n#\n# ### 3. HTTP API (Optional)\n#\n# To use the HTTP API, you must install the `api` extra dependencies (e.g., `pip install \".[api]\"` or `poetry install -E api`).\n#\n# **Start the API server:**\n#\n# ```bash\n# uvicorn car_collision_app.controllers.api_controller:get_app --factory --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000\n# ```\n#\n# **Make a request (e.g., using `curl`):**\n#\n# ```bash\n# curl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"n\": 7}' http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/collision\n# # Output: {\"n\":7,\"collisions\":49}\n# ```\n#\n# For invalid input:\n#\n# ```bash\n# curl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"n\": -2}' http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/collision\n# # Output: {\"detail\":\"n must be a non-negative integer\"}\n# ```\n#\n# ## Development\n#\n# **Run tests:**\n# ```bash\n# poetry run pytest\n# ```\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/__init__.py\n# Package initialization.\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/config.py\n# Configuration constants for the application.\n\nDEFAULT_PORT: int = 8000\nDEFAULT_HOST: str = \"127.0.0.1\"\nAPI_PREFIX: str = \"/api\"\nCLI_EXIT_INVALID_INPUT: int = 2\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/exceptions.py\n# Defines custom exception types for the application.\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input values.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, code: int = 400) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n        self.code = code\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/models/car_race_request.py\n# Data Transfer Object (DTO) for car race requests.\n\nclass CarRaceRequest:\n    \"\"\"A DTO to encapsulate the request parameter 'n'.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n: int) -> None:\n        self.n: int = n\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Converts the DTO to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\"n\": self.n}\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/utils/validators.py\n# Utility functions for validating input.\n\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom ..exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef validate_n(value: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Validates and coerces 'n' to a non-negative integer.\n\n    Raises InvalidInputError if the value is not a valid non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(value, int):\n        if value < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be a non-negative integer\")\n        return value\n    if isinstance(value, str):\n        if value.isdigit(): # Checks if all characters are digits and there is at least one character\n            int_value = int(value)\n            if int_value < 0: # This case is covered by isdigit() indirectly, but for robustness\n                raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be a non-negative integer\")\n            return int_value\n    raise InvalidInputError(\"n must be a non-negative integer\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/services/collision_service.py\n# Core service for collision computation.\n\nfrom ..models.car_race_request import CarRaceRequest\n\nclass CollisionService:\n    \"\"\"Provides core collision computation logic.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        pass\n\n    def collision_count(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the number of collisions for 'n' cars per side.\n\n        Assumes 'n' is a validated non-negative integer.\n        \"\"\"\n        return n * n\n\n    def compute_from_request(self, request: CarRaceRequest) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes collisions from a CarRaceRequest DTO.\"\"\"\n        return self.collision_count(request.n)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/controllers/cli_controller.py\n# Handles command-line interface logic.\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, TextIO\n\nfrom ..services.collision_service import CollisionService\nfrom ..utils.validators import validate_n\nfrom ..models.car_race_request import CarRaceRequest\nfrom ..exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .. import config\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Manages command-line argument parsing and execution.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: CollisionService, out: TextIO = sys.stdout, err: TextIO = sys.stderr) -> None:\n        self.service = service\n        self.out = out\n        self.err = err\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the CLI command based on provided arguments.\n\n        Parses 'n', validates, computes, and prints the result or an error message.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            if len(argv) < 2:\n                raise InvalidInputError(\"Usage: car-collision <n>\")\n            n_str = argv[1]\n            n = validate_n(n_str)\n            req = CarRaceRequest(n)\n            res = self.service.compute_from_request(req)\n            print(res, file=self.out)\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e.message}\", file=self.err)\n            return config.CLI_EXIT_INVALID_INPUT\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=self.err)\n            return 1 # General error code\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/controllers/api_controller.py\n# Handles HTTP API routing and request processing.\n\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nfrom ..services.collision_service import CollisionService\nfrom ..utils.validators import validate_n\nfrom ..models.car_race_request import CarRaceRequest\nfrom ..exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .. import config\n\nclass NPayload(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Pydantic model for the request payload.\"\"\"\n    n: Any = Field(..., description=\"Number of cars per side (non-negative integer).\")\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Manages the FastAPI application and HTTP routes.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: CollisionService) -> None:\n        self.service = service\n        self.app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"Car Collision API\",\n            description=\"API for computing car collisions (n^2).\",\n            version=\"0.1.0\",\n        )\n        # Mount the API routes\n        self.app.post(f\"{config.API_PREFIX}/collision\", response_model=dict)(self._post_collision)\n        self.app.get(\"/health\", status_code=200, response_model=dict)(self._health_check)\n\n    def _post_collision(self, payload: NPayload) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Handles POST requests to compute collisions.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            n = validate_n(payload.n)\n            req = CarRaceRequest(n)\n            collisions = self.service.compute_from_request(req)\n            return {\"n\": n, \"collisions\": collisions}\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=e.message)\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=f\"Internal server error: {e}\")\n\n    def _health_check(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Provides a simple health check endpoint.\"\"\"\n        return {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n    def get_app(self) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"Returns the configured FastAPI application instance.\"\"\"\n        return self.app\n\n# Function to be used by uvicorn --factory option\ndef get_app() -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"Factory function to create a FastAPI app instance for uvicorn.\"\"\"\n    service = CollisionService()\n    controller = APIController(service)\n    return controller.get_app()\n```\n\n```python\n# src/car_collision_app/main.py\n# Main entrypoint for the CLI console script.\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Optional, List\n\nfrom .services.collision_service import CollisionService\nfrom .controllers.cli_controller import CLIController\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the car-collision CLI command.\n\n    Initializes the service and controller, then runs the CLI.\n    \"\"\"\n    if argv is None:\n        argv = sys.argv\n    \n    service = CollisionService()\n    controller = CLIController(service)\n    return controller.run(argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_collision_service.py\n# Unit tests for the CollisionService.\n\nimport pytest\nfrom car_collision_app.services.collision_service import CollisionService\nfrom car_collision_app.models.car_race_request import CarRaceRequest\n\ndef test_collision_count_zero_cars():\n    \"\"\"Tests collision count for zero cars.\"\"\"\n    service = CollisionService()\n    assert service.collision_count(0) == 0\n\ndef test_collision_count_positive_n():\n    \"\"\"Tests collision count for a positive number of cars.\"\"\"\n    service = CollisionService()\n    assert service.collision_count(1) == 1\n    assert service.collision_count(5) == 25\n    assert service.collision_count(10) == 100\n\ndef test_collision_count_large_n():\n    \"\"\"Tests collision count for a large number of cars.\"\"\"\n    service = CollisionService()\n    assert service.collision_count(1000) == 1_000_000\n    assert service.collision_count(10**6) == 10**12\n\ndef test_compute_from_request():\n    \"\"\"Tests computing collisions using a CarRaceRequest.\"\"\"\n    service = CollisionService()\n    request = CarRaceRequest(n=3)\n    assert service.compute_from_request(request) == 9\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_validators.py\n# Unit tests for the input validators.\n\nimport pytest\nfrom car_collision_app.utils.validators import validate_n\nfrom car_collision_app.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef test_validate_n_valid_int():\n    \"\"\"Tests validate_n with a valid integer.\"\"\"\n    assert validate_n(5) == 5\n    assert validate_n(0) == 0\n    assert validate_n(1000) == 1000\n\ndef test_validate_n_valid_numeric_string():\n    \"\"\"Tests validate_n with a valid numeric string.\"\"\"\n    assert validate_n(\"10\") == 10\n    assert validate_n(\"0\") == 0\n    assert validate_n(\"999\") == 999\n\ndef test_validate_n_negative_int():\n    \"\"\"Tests validate_n with a negative integer, expecting an error.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n(-1)\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n(-100)\n\ndef test_validate_n_negative_numeric_string():\n    \"\"\"Tests validate_n with a negative numeric string, expecting an error.\"\"\"\n    # isdigit() check prevents this, but for explicit testing, ensuring it's caught\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n(\"-5\")\n\ndef test_validate_n_non_numeric_string():\n    \"\"\"Tests validate_n with a non-numeric string, expecting an error.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n(\"abc\")\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n(\"10.5\") # Float string\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n(\"\")\n\ndef test_validate_n_invalid_type():\n    \"\"\"Tests validate_n with invalid types, expecting an error.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n(None)\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n(3.14)\n    with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"n must be a non-negative integer\"):\n        validate_n([1, 2])\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_cli.py\n# Integration tests for the CLIController.\n\nimport pytest\nfrom io import StringIO\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom car_collision_app.services.collision_service import CollisionService\nfrom car_collision_app.controllers.cli_controller import CLIController\nfrom car_collision_app import config\n\n# Fixture to provide a CLIController instance with mocked stdout/stderr\n@pytest.fixture\ndef cli_controller():\n    \"\"\"Provides a CLIController with in-memory output streams for testing.\"\"\"\n    service = CollisionService()\n    return CLIController(service, out=StringIO(), err=StringIO())\n\ndef test_cli_success(cli_controller):\n    \"\"\"Tests successful CLI execution with a valid input.\"\"\"\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"car-collision\", \"5\"])\n    assert exit_code == 0\n    assert cli_controller.out.getvalue().strip() == \"25\"\n    assert cli_controller.err.getvalue().strip() == \"\"\n\ndef test_cli_success_zero_input(cli_controller):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI execution with zero input.\"\"\"\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"car-collision\", \"0\"])\n    assert exit_code == 0\n    assert cli_controller.out.getvalue().strip() == \"0\"\n    assert cli_controller.err.getvalue().strip() == \"\"\n\ndef test_cli_invalid_negative_input(cli_controller):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI execution with a negative input.\"\"\"\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"car-collision\", \"-5\"])\n    assert exit_code == config.CLI_EXIT_INVALID_INPUT\n    assert cli_controller.out.getvalue().strip() == \"\"\n    assert \"Error: n must be a non-negative integer\" in cli_controller.err.getvalue().strip()\n\ndef test_cli_invalid_non_numeric_input(cli_controller):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI execution with non-numeric input.\"\"\"\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"car-collision\", \"abc\"])\n    assert exit_code == config.CLI_EXIT_INVALID_INPUT\n    assert cli_controller.out.getvalue().strip() == \"\"\n    assert \"Error: n must be a non-negative integer\" in cli_controller.err.getvalue().strip()\n\ndef test_cli_missing_argument(cli_controller):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI execution when argument is missing.\"\"\"\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"car-collision\"])\n    assert exit_code == config.CLI_EXIT_INVALID_INPUT\n    assert cli_controller.out.getvalue().strip() == \"\"\n    assert \"Error: Usage: car-collision <n>\" in cli_controller.err.getvalue().strip()\n\ndef test_cli_multiple_arguments_ignores_extra(cli_controller):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI execution with multiple arguments (only first is used).\"\"\"\n    exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"car-collision\", \"3\", \"extra\"])\n    assert exit_code == 0\n    assert cli_controller.out.getvalue().strip() == \"9\"\n    assert cli_controller.err.getvalue().strip() == \"\"\n\ndef test_cli_unexpected_error(cli_controller):\n    \"\"\"Tests CLI execution with an unexpected internal error.\"\"\"\n    with patch.object(cli_controller.service, 'compute_from_request', side_effect=ValueError(\"Test Error\")):\n        exit_code = cli_controller.run([\"car-collision\", \"2\"])\n        assert exit_code == 1 # General error code\n        assert cli_controller.out.getvalue().strip() == \"\"\n        assert \"An unexpected error occurred: Test Error\" in cli_controller.err.getvalue().strip()\n```\n```python\n# tests/test_api.py\n# Integration tests for the APIController using FastAPI's TestClient.\n# This file is only required if FastAPI and uvicorn are installed.\n\nimport pytest\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient\nfrom car_collision_app.controllers.api_controller import get_app # Import the factory function\n\n# Fixture to create a test client for the FastAPI app\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")\ndef client():\n    \"\"\"Provides a FastAPI TestClient instance for API integration tests.\"\"\"\n    app = get_app()\n    with TestClient(app) as c:\n        yield c\n\ndef test_api_post_collision_success(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests successful POST /api/collision with valid input.\"\"\"\n    response = client.post(\"/api/collision\", json={\"n\": 7})\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.json() == {\"n\": 7, \"collisions\": 49}\n\ndef test_api_post_collision_zero(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/collision with n=0.\"\"\"\n    response = client.post(\"/api/collision\", json={\"n\": 0})\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.json() == {\"n\": 0, \"collisions\": 0}\n\ndef test_api_post_collision_large_n(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/collision with a large n.\"\"\"\n    response = client.post(\"/api/collision\", json={\"n\": 1000})\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.json() == {\"n\": 1000, \"collisions\": 1_000_000}\n\ndef test_api_post_collision_invalid_negative_n(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/collision with a negative n.\"\"\"\n    response = client.post(\"/api/collision\", json={\"n\": -5})\n    assert response.status_code == 400\n    assert response.json() == {\"detail\": \"n must be a non-negative integer\"}\n\ndef test_api_post_collision_invalid_non_numeric_n(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/collision with non-numeric n.\"\"\"\n    response = client.post(\"/api/collision\", json={\"n\": \"abc\"})\n    assert response.status_code == 400\n    assert response.json() == {\"detail\": \"n must be a non-negative integer\"}\n\ndef test_api_post_collision_invalid_float_n(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/collision with a float n.\"\"\"\n    response = client.post(\"/api/collision\", json={\"n\": 3.14})\n    assert response.status_code == 400\n    assert response.json() == {\"detail\": \"n must be a non-negative integer\"}\n\ndef test_api_post_collision_missing_n(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/collision with missing n.\"\"\"\n    response = client.post(\"/api/collision\", json={})\n    assert response.status_code == 422 # FastAPI's validation error for missing field\n    assert \"field required\" in response.json()[\"detail\"][0][\"msg\"]\n\ndef test_api_post_collision_unexpected_error(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests POST /api/collision for an unexpected internal server error.\"\"\"\n    # Mocking the service method to raise an unexpected error\n    with patch.object(CollisionService, 'compute_from_request', side_effect=RuntimeError(\"Service failure\")):\n        response = client.post(\"/api/collision\", json={\"n\": 2})\n        assert response.status_code == 500\n        assert response.json() == {\"detail\": \"Internal server error: Service failure\"}\n\ndef test_api_health_check(client):\n    \"\"\"Tests the /health endpoint.\"\"\"\n    response = client.get(\"/health\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.json() == {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n```"}
