{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/__init__.py\n\"\"\"Package init, exports public API.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .encoder import ShiftEncoder\nfrom .services import ShiftService\nfrom .cli import main as cli_main\nfrom .api import create_app\n\n__all__ = [\"ShiftEncoder\", \"ShiftService\", \"cli_main\", \"create_app\"]\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/config.py\n\"\"\"App configuration constants and loader.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nDEFAULT_SHIFT: int = 5\nHISTORY_FILE: str = \"./data/history.json\"\nAPI_KEY_ENV: str = \"SHIFT_CIPHER_API_KEY\"\nMAX_HISTORY_ITEMS: int = 1000\n\ndef load_api_key() -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Loads the API key from environment variable.\"\"\"\n    return os.getenv(API_KEY_ENV)\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"Domain-specific exceptions for validation and storage errors.\"\"\"\n\nclass ShiftCipherError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for Shift Cipher operations.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass ValidationError(ShiftCipherError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when input validation fails.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass StorageError(ShiftCipherError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when there are issues with history persistence.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/utils.py\n\"\"\"Helper functions for validation and atomic file operations.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nimport re\nimport tempfile\n\ndef validate_alpha(s: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string contains only lowercase ASCII letters.\"\"\"\n    return bool(re.fullmatch(r\"^[a-z]+$\", s))\n\ndef sanitize_input(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Placeholder for future sanitization; currently returns string as is.\"\"\"\n    # Based on current requirements, input must be [a-z] already,\n    # so actual sanitization would involve error or stripping,\n    # but design specifies ValidationError for invalid chars.\n    return s\n\ndef atomic_write(path: str, data: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Atomically writes data to a file using a temporary file and rename.\"\"\"\n    # Ensure the directory exists\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path) or '.', exist_ok=True)\n    \n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode=\"w\", delete=False, encoding=\"utf-8\") as tmp_file:\n        tmp_file.write(data)\n    os.rename(tmp_file.name, path)\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/models.py\n\"\"\"DTOs and domain models for the Shift Cipher application.\"\"\"\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\nfrom typing import List, Literal, Optional\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_SHIFT\n\nclass MessageRecord(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Represents a historical record of an encode/decode operation.\"\"\"\n    id: str\n    timestamp: str\n    operation: Literal[\"encode\", \"decode\"]\n    input: str\n    shift: int\n    result: str\n\nclass EncodeRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Request model for encode/decode API operations.\"\"\"\n    text: str = Field(..., description=\"Lowercase alphabetic string to process.\")\n    shift: Optional[int] = Field(DEFAULT_SHIFT, ge=1, le=25,\n                                 description=\"Shift value (1-25).\")\n    save: bool = Field(False, description=\"Whether to save the operation to history.\")\n\nclass EncodeResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Response model for encode/decode API operations.\"\"\"\n    result: str\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/encoder.py\n\"\"\"ShiftEncoder: pure algorithmic implementation of encode/decode.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_SHIFT\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .utils import validate_alpha\n\nclass ShiftEncoder:\n    \"\"\"Handles Caesar-style shifting for encoding and decoding.\"\"\"\n\n    def encode(self, text: str, shift: int = DEFAULT_SHIFT) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Shifts each lowercase letter forward by 'shift' positions.\"\"\"\n        if not validate_alpha(text):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input text must contain only lowercase a-z.\")\n        if not (1 <= shift <= 25):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Shift value must be an integer between 1 and 25.\")\n\n        encoded_chars = []\n        for char in text:\n            # ord('a') = 97\n            shifted_char_code = ((ord(char) - ord('a') + shift) % 26) + ord('a')\n            encoded_chars.append(chr(shifted_char_code))\n        return \"\".join(encoded_chars)\n\n    def decode(self, text: str, shift: int = DEFAULT_SHIFT) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Shifts each lowercase letter backward by 'shift' positions.\"\"\"\n        # Decoding is equivalent to encoding with (26 - shift)\n        return self.encode(text, shift=26 - (shift % 26))\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/repositories.py\n\"\"\"HistoryRepository: file-based JSON persistence adapter.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .models import MessageRecord\nfrom .exceptions import StorageError\nfrom .utils import atomic_write\nfrom .config import MAX_HISTORY_ITEMS\n\nclass HistoryRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages persistence of MessageRecord objects to a local JSON file.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, path: str):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the repository with the history file path.\"\"\"\n        self.path = path\n        # Ensure the directory exists upon initialization\n        if self.path:\n            # Using path.split('/')[0] or os.path.dirname(path) to get directory\n            # but for simple \"./data/history.json\" '.' will be dir, or 'data'\n            # atomic_write will create the dir if not exists, but better to check on init.\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path) or '.', exist_ok=True)\n\n    def save(self, record: MessageRecord) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a MessageRecord atomically to the JSON array in the file.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            current_data = self._read_history()\n            current_data.append(record.dict())\n            \n            # Limit history size to prevent unbounded growth\n            if len(current_data) > MAX_HISTORY_ITEMS:\n                current_data = current_data[-MAX_HISTORY_ITEMS:]\n            \n            atomic_write(self.path, json.dumps(current_data, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\n        except (OSError, IOError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n            raise StorageError(f\"Failed to save history: {exc}\")\n\n    def list(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[MessageRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the last N history entries from the file.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            data = self._read_history()\n            return [MessageRecord(**r) for r in data][-limit:]\n        except (OSError, IOError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n            raise StorageError(f\"Failed to load history: {exc}\")\n\n    def _read_history(self) -> List[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Helper to read and parse the history file.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            with open(self.path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                return json.load(f)\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            return []\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            # Handle corrupted or empty JSON by starting fresh\n            return []\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/services.py\n\"\"\"ShiftService: orchestrates encoding/decoding and history persistence.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom uuid import uuid4\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nfrom .encoder import ShiftEncoder\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom .models import MessageRecord\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_SHIFT\n\nclass ShiftService:\n    \"\"\"Provides application logic for Caesar cipher operations and history management.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, encoder: ShiftEncoder, repo: HistoryRepository, default_shift: int = DEFAULT_SHIFT):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the ShiftService with an encoder, repository, and default shift.\"\"\"\n        self.encoder = encoder\n        self.repo = repo\n        self.default_shift = default_shift\n\n    def encode(self, text: str, shift: Optional[int] = None, save: bool = False) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Encodes a string using the Caesar cipher, optionally saving the operation.\"\"\"\n        actual_shift = shift if shift is not None else self.default_shift\n        result = self.encoder.encode(text, actual_shift)\n        if save:\n            record = MessageRecord(\n                id=str(uuid4()),\n                timestamp=datetime.utcnow().isoformat(timespec='seconds') + \"Z\",\n                operation=\"encode\",\n                input=text,\n                shift=actual_shift,\n                result=result\n            )\n            self.repo.save(record)\n        return result\n\n    def decode(self, text: str, shift: Optional[int] = None, save: bool = False) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Decodes a string using the Caesar cipher, optionally saving the operation.\"\"\"\n        actual_shift = shift if shift is not None else self.default_shift\n        result = self.encoder.decode(text, actual_shift)\n        if save:\n            record = MessageRecord(\n                id=str(uuid4()),\n                timestamp=datetime.utcnow().isoformat(timespec='seconds') + \"Z\",\n                operation=\"decode\",\n                input=text,\n                shift=actual_shift,\n                result=result\n            )\n            self.repo.save(record)\n        return result\n\n    def get_history(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[MessageRecord]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves recent operation history entries.\"\"\"\n        return self.repo.list(limit)\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/cli.py\n\"\"\"CLIController: command-line interface entrypoint using argparse.\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_SHIFT, HISTORY_FILE\nfrom .encoder import ShiftEncoder\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom .services import ShiftService\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, StorageError\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Manages command-line interactions for the Shift Cipher application.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, service: ShiftService):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLIController with a ShiftService instance.\"\"\"\n        self.service = service\n\n    def _parse_args(self, argv: List[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:\n        \"\"\"Parses command-line arguments using argparse.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"shiftcipher\",\n            description=\"Encode or decode strings using a Caesar-style shift.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"operation\",\n            choices=[\"encode\", \"decode\"],\n            help=\"Operation to perform: 'encode' or 'decode'.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"text\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"The string to be encoded or decoded (lowercase a-z only).\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--shift\",\n            type=int,\n            default=DEFAULT_SHIFT,\n            choices=range(1, 26),\n            metavar=\"N\",\n            help=f\"The shift value (1-25, default: {DEFAULT_SHIFT}).\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--save\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Save the operation to history.\"\n        )\n        return parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    def main(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Main entrypoint for the CLI application.\"\"\"\n        args = self._parse_args(argv[1:])\n\n        try:\n            if args.operation == \"encode\":\n                result = self.service.encode(args.text, args.shift, args.save)\n            else: # decode\n                result = self.service.decode(args.text, args.shift, args.save)\n            print(result)\n            return 0\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Validation error exit code\n        except StorageError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3 # Storage error exit code\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # General error exit code\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the shiftcipher CLI command.\"\"\"\n    encoder = ShiftEncoder()\n    repo = HistoryRepository(HISTORY_FILE)\n    service = ShiftService(encoder, repo, DEFAULT_SHIFT)\n    controller = CLIController(service)\n    sys.exit(controller.main(sys.argv))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```python\n# File: src/shiftcipher/api.py\n\"\"\"APIController: FastAPI app exposing endpoints.\"\"\"\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Header, Depends, status\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse\nfrom typing import Optional, List\n\nfrom .config import HISTORY_FILE, API_KEY_ENV, DEFAULT_SHIFT\nfrom .encoder import ShiftEncoder\nfrom .repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom .services import ShiftService\nfrom .models import EncodeRequest, EncodeResponse, MessageRecord\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, StorageError\nfrom .config import load_api_key\n\ndef get_service(repo: Optional[HistoryRepository] = None) -> ShiftService:\n    \"\"\"Dependency injector for ShiftService.\"\"\"\n    repository = repo or HistoryRepository(HISTORY_FILE)\n    encoder = ShiftEncoder()\n    return ShiftService(encoder, repository, DEFAULT_SHIFT)\n\ndef create_app(service: Optional[ShiftService] = None) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"Builds and returns the FastAPI application instance.\"\"\"\n    app = FastAPI(\n        title=\"Shift Cipher Service\",\n        description=\"A simple API for Caesar-style string encoding/decoding and history.\",\n        version=\"0.1.0\"\n    )\n\n    # Lazily create service if not provided (for production/testing setup flexibility)\n    if service is None:\n        service = get_service()\n\n    # Authentication dependency\n    api_key_env = load_api_key()\n    def require_api_key(x_api_key: Optional[str] = Header(None, alias=\"X-API-Key\")):\n        \"\"\"Authenticates requests using an optional API key from environment.\"\"\"\n        if api_key_env and (not x_api_key or x_api_key != api_key_env):\n            raise HTTPException(\n                status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n                detail=\"Invalid API Key.\"\n            )\n\n    @app.post(\"/encode\", response_model=EncodeResponse, tags=[\"Operations\"])\n    async def encode_endpoint(\n        request: EncodeRequest,\n        service: ShiftService = Depends(get_service),\n        auth: None = Depends(require_api_key)\n    ):\n        \"\"\"Encodes a string using the Caesar cipher.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            result = service.encode(request.text, request.shift, request.save)\n            return EncodeResponse(result=result)\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e))\n        except StorageError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=str(e))\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"An unexpected error occurred.\")\n\n    @app.post(\"/decode\", response_model=EncodeResponse, tags=[\"Operations\"])\n    async def decode_endpoint(\n        request: EncodeRequest,\n        service: ShiftService = Depends(get_service),\n        auth: None = Depends(require_api_key)\n    ):\n        \"\"\"Decodes a string previously encoded with the Caesar cipher.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            result = service.decode(request.text, request.shift, request.save)\n            return EncodeResponse(result=result)\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e))\n        except StorageError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=str(e))\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"An unexpected error occurred.\")\n\n    @app.get(\"/history\", response_model=List[MessageRecord], tags=[\"History\"])\n    async def get_history_endpoint(\n        limit: int = 100,\n        service: ShiftService = Depends(get_service),\n        auth: None = Depends(require_api_key)\n    ):\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of recent encode/decode operations from history.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            return service.get_history(limit)\n        except StorageError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=str(e))\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"An unexpected error occurred.\")\n\n    return app\n\n# When running this file directly with uvicorn (e.g., `uvicorn src.shiftcipher.api:app`),\n# FastAPI looks for an `app` variable.\napp = create_app()\n\n```python\n# File: pyproject.toml\n\"\"\"Build config, dependencies for the project.\"\"\"\n\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"shiftcipher\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reliable library and service to encode and decode alphabetical strings using a Caesar-style shift.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"shiftcipher\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.10,<4.0\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.29.0\"}\npydantic = \"^2.7.1\"\nargparse = \"^1.4.0\" # argparse is built-in but can be listed if desired for explicit clarity or older python compatibility (not here)\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.1\"\nblack = \"^24.4.2\"\nflake8 = \"^7.0.0\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nshiftcipher = \"shiftcipher.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```python\n# File: README.md\n\"\"\"Usage and examples for the Shift Cipher service.\"\"\"\n\n# Shift Cipher Service\n\nThis project provides a Python library, a Command-Line Interface (CLI), and an HTTP API for encoding and decoding alphabetical strings using a Caesar-style shift cipher. It supports customizable shift values and maintains an appendable history of operations.\n\n## Features\n\n-   **Library:** Python functions for `encode` and `decode`.\n-   **CLI:** Command-line tool for quick encode/decode operations.\n-   **HTTP API:** RESTful JSON API using FastAPI.\n-   **History:** Operations can be saved to a local JSON file for audit.\n-   **Validation:** Strict input validation for lowercase `a-z` characters.\n\n## Installation\n\nThis project uses [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/) for dependency management.\n\n1.  **Clone the repository:**\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/your-username/shiftcipher.git\n    cd shiftcipher\n    ```\n2.  **Install dependencies:**\n    ```bash\n    poetry install\n    ```\n3.  **Activate the virtual environment:**\n    ```bash\n    poetry shell\n    ```\n\n## Usage\n\n### 1. Library\n\nYou can use the `ShiftEncoder` and `ShiftService` classes directly in your Python code.\n\n```python\nfrom src.shiftcipher.encoder import ShiftEncoder\nfrom src.shiftcipher.repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom src.shiftcipher.services import ShiftService\nfrom src.shiftcipher.config import HISTORY_FILE\n\n# Initialize components\nencoder = ShiftEncoder()\nrepo = HistoryRepository(HISTORY_FILE)\nservice = ShiftService(encoder, repo)\n\n# Encode a string\nencoded_text = service.encode(\"hello\", shift=3)\nprint(f\"Encoded 'hello' with shift 3: {encoded_text}\") # Output: 'khoor'\n\n# Decode a string\ndecoded_text = service.decode(\"khoor\", shift=3)\nprint(f\"Decoded 'khoor' with shift 3: {decoded_text}\") # Output: 'hello'\n\n# Encode and save to history\nservice.encode(\"world\", shift=5, save=True)\n\n# Retrieve history\nhistory = service.get_history(limit=5)\nfor record in history:\n    print(record.dict())\n```\n\n### 2. Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nThe CLI tool `shiftcipher` is available after installation.\n\n**Encode a string:**\n\n```bash\nshiftcipher encode hello\n# Output: mjqqt\n```\n\n**Encode with a custom shift:**\n\n```bash\nshiftcipher encode hello --shift 3\n# Output: khoor\n```\n\n**Decode a string:**\n\n```bash\nshiftcipher decode mjqqt\n# Output: hello\n```\n\n**Decode with a custom shift:**\n\n```bash\nshiftcipher decode khoor --shift 3\n# Output: hello\n```\n\n**Save operation to history:**\n\n```bash\nshiftcipher encode goodbye --shift 2 --save\n```\n\n### 3. HTTP API\n\nThe HTTP API is built with FastAPI.\n\n**Run the API service:**\n\n```bash\npoetry run uvicorn src.shiftcipher.api:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThe API will be accessible at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`. You can then interact with it using tools like `curl` or Postman.\n\n**API Endpoints:**\n\n-   **POST /encode**\n    -   **Request Body (JSON):**\n        ```json\n        {\n          \"text\": \"hello\",\n          \"shift\": 5,\n          \"save\": true\n        }\n        ```\n    -   **Response Body (JSON):**\n        ```json\n        {\n          \"result\": \"mjqqt\"\n        }\n        ```\n-   **POST /decode**\n    -   **Request Body (JSON):** Same as `/encode`.\n    -   **Response Body (JSON):**\n        ```json\n        {\n          \"result\": \"hello\"\n        }\n        ```\n-   **GET /history**\n    -   **Query Parameters:** `limit` (optional, integer, default 100)\n    -   **Response Body (JSON):**\n        ```json\n        [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"...\",\n            \"timestamp\": \"2023-10-27T10:00:00Z\",\n            \"operation\": \"encode\",\n            \"input\": \"hello\",\n            \"shift\": 5,\n            \"result\": \"mjqqt\"\n          }\n        ]\n        ```\n\n**API Key Authentication (Optional):**\n\nIf the environment variable `SHIFT_CIPHER_API_KEY` is set, API endpoints will require an `X-API-Key` header with the correct value.\n\n```bash\nexport SHIFT_CIPHER_API_KEY=\"mysecretkey\"\ncurl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/encode\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -H \"X-API-Key: mysecretkey\" \\\n     -d '{\"text\": \"test\", \"shift\": 1}'\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 shiftcipher/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py      # Package exports\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 config.py        # Application configuration\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 encoder.py       # Core encoding/decoding logic\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py      # Application logic and orchestration\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 repositories.py  # History persistence (JSON file)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py        # Data models (Pydantic)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py    # Custom exceptions\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py         # Helper functions (validation, atomic writes)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli.py           # Command-Line Interface entrypoint\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 api.py           # HTTP API entrypoint (FastAPI)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 data/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 history.json         # Default history file (auto-generated)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/                   # (Not included in this generation, but part of design)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml           # Project metadata and dependencies (Poetry)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md                # This file\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 .github/                 # GitHub Actions CI workflow (not included in this generation)\n```\n\n## Development and Testing\n\nThe design specifies unit and integration tests, but these are not generated here.\nTo run tests (if implemented): `poetry run pytest`\n\n## CI/CD (Example Workflow)\n\n(A `.github/workflows/ci.yml` would typically be provided to set up GitHub Actions for running tests and linting.)\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [ main ]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [ main ]\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.10\", \"3.11\", \"3.12\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n        cache: 'poetry'\n    - name: Install Poetry\n      run: pip install poetry\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: poetry install --no-root\n    - name: Lint with flake8\n      run: |\n        # stop the build if there are Python syntax errors or undefined names\n        flake8 src/shiftcipher --count --select=E9,F63,F7,F82 --show-source --statistics\n        # exit-zero treats all errors as warnings. The GitHub editor is 1-indexed, so line numbers for warnings are shown one less than they actually are.\n        flake8 src/shiftcipher --count --exit-zero --max-complexity=10 --max-line-length=120 --statistics\n    - name: Format with black (check only)\n      run: black src/shiftcipher --check\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: poetry run pytest # Assumes tests are in `tests/` directory\n```\n\n## Data Persistence\n\nOperation history is stored in a JSON file (default `./data/history.json`). The file is an array of JSON objects, each representing a `MessageRecord`. Atomic writes are used to prevent data corruption.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n-   **`ValidationError`**: Ensure input strings contain only lowercase `a-z` characters and the shift value is between 1 and 25.\n-   **`StorageError`**: Check file permissions for the `data/` directory and `history.json` file.\n-   **API 401 Unauthorized**: If `SHIFT_CIPHER_API_KEY` is set, ensure you provide the correct `X-API-Key` header.\n-   **API 500 Internal Server Error**: Check server logs for detailed error messages, often indicating a `StorageError`.\n\n---\n```\n```\n```\n```\n```"}
