bash\npoetry run arith-add 5 3\n# Output: 8\n\npoetry run arith-add 100 -200\n# Output: -100\n\npoetry run arith-add hello world\n# Output: Error: Invalid integer: 'hello'\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\n1.  **Start the API server:**\n    ```bash\n    poetry run arith-api\n    # INFO:     Uvicorn running on http://127.0.0.1:8000 (Press CTRL+C to quit)\n    ```\n    The server will run on `http://127.0.0.1:8000` by default. You can configure host/port using environment variables (`ARITH_API_HOST`, `ARITH_API_PORT`).\n\n2.  **Perform an addition (e.g., using `curl`):**\n    ```bash\n    curl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"x\": 10, \"y\": 15}' http://127.0.0.1:8000/add\n    # Output: {\"result\":25}\n    ```\n\n3.  **Retrieve operation history:**\n    ```bash\n    curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/history?limit=2\n    # Output: {\"history\":[{\"id\":1,\"timestamp\":\"...\",\"x\":10,\"y\":15,\"result\":25}, ...]}\n    ```\n\n### Configuration\n\nYou can configure the application using environment variables:\n\n-   `ARITH_DB_PATH`: Path to the SQLite database file (default: `./data/history.db`).\n-   `ARITH_API_HOST`: API server host (default: `127.0.0.1`).\n-   `ARITH_API_PORT`: API server port (default: `8000`).\n\nExample:\n```bash\nARITH_DB_PATH=./custom.db ARITH_API_PORT=5000 poetry run arith-api\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 arithmetic/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 config.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 validator.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 add_operation.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 calculator_service.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 history_repository.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 api_controller.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli.py\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 utils.py\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 data/\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 (history.db created at runtime)\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\nTo run all tests (including doctests):\n\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\n### Linting\n\n```bash\npoetry run flake8 src\n```\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/__init__.py\n\"\"\"Package init: exports factory functions and version.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .models import OperationModel\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .validator import Validator\nfrom .add_operation import AddOperation\nfrom .calculator_service import CalculatorService\nfrom .history_repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom .api_controller import APIController\nfrom .cli import CLIController\nfrom .utils import iso_timestamp, configure_logging\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\ndef _get_calculator_service_instance():\n    \"\"\"Returns a new CalculatorService instance configured from environment.\"\"\"\n    cfg = Config.from_env()\n    repo = HistoryRepository(cfg.db_path)\n    validator = Validator()\n    return CalculatorService(repo, validator)\n\n# This wrapper function hosts the original doctest as specified.\n# It uses the CalculatorService for consistency with the design.\ndef add(x: int, y: int):\n    \"\"\"Add two numbers x and y.\n    >>> add(2, 3)\n    5\n    >>> add(5, 7)\n    12\n    \"\"\"\n    service = _get_calculator_service_instance()\n    # The doctest inputs are guaranteed ints, matching CalculatorService's internal validation.\n    return service.add(x, y)\n\n# Expose an instance of the service for direct programmatic use.\ncalculator_service_instance = _get_calculator_service_instance()\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"__version__\",\n    \"Config\",\n    \"OperationModel\",\n    \"ValidationError\",\n    \"PersistenceError\",\n    \"Validator\",\n    \"AddOperation\",\n    \"CalculatorService\",\n    \"HistoryRepository\",\n    \"APIController\",\n    \"CLIController\",\n    \"iso_timestamp\",\n    \"configure_logging\",\n    \"add\", # The wrapper for doctests\n    \"calculator_service_instance\",\n]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/config.py\n\"\"\"Central configuration values, loaded from environment variables.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Config:\n    \"\"\"Configuration settings for the application.\"\"\"\n    db_path: str\n    api_host: str\n    api_port: int\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_env() -> \"Config\":\n        \"\"\"Builds a Config object by reading environment variables.\"\"\"\n        db_path = os.getenv(\"ARITH_DB_PATH\", \"./data/history.db\")\n        api_host = os.getenv(\"ARITH_API_HOST\", \"127.0.0.1\")\n        api_port = int(os.getenv(\"ARITH_API_PORT\", \"8000\"))\n        return Config(db_path=db_path, api_host=api_host, api_port=api_port)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/models.py\n\"\"\"Domain models for operations.\"\"\"\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass OperationModel:\n    \"\"\"Represents a persisted arithmetic operation record.\"\"\"\n    id: int | None\n    timestamp: str\n    x: int\n    y: int\n    result: int\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Converts the OperationModel instance to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"id\": self.id,\n            \"timestamp\": self.timestamp,\n            \"x\": self.x,\n            \"y\": self.y,\n            \"result\": self.result,\n        }\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"Custom domain-level exceptions for the arithmetic library.\"\"\"\n\nclass ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when input validation fails.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass PersistenceError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a database persistence operation fails.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/validator.py\n\"\"\"Utility class for input validation.\"\"\"\n\nimport re\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass Validator:\n    \"\"\"Provides methods for validating and coercing various input types.\"\"\"\n    _int_re = re.compile(r\"^[+-]?\\d+$\")\n\n    def validate_int(self, value: Any) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Validates if a value can be converted to an integer.\"\"\"\n        if isinstance(value, int):\n            return value\n        if isinstance(value, str) and self._int_re.match(value.strip()):\n            return int(value.strip())\n        raise ValidationError(f\"Invalid integer: {value!r}\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/add_operation.py\n\"\"\"Encapsulates the addition operation.\"\"\"\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass AddOperation:\n    \"\"\"Represents an addition operation with two integer operands.\"\"\"\n    x: int\n    y: int\n    result: int | None = None\n\n    def compute(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Performs the addition and stores the result.\"\"\"\n        self.result = self.x + self.y\n        return self.result\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/calculator_service.py\n\"\"\"Business logic and orchestration for arithmetic operations.\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Any, List\nfrom .add_operation import AddOperation\nfrom .models import OperationModel\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\nfrom .history_repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom .validator import Validator\nfrom .utils import iso_timestamp\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass CalculatorService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates validation, operation execution, and persistence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repo: HistoryRepository, validator: Validator) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CalculatorService with a repository and validator.\"\"\"\n        self._repo = repo\n        self._validator = validator\n\n    def add(self, x: Any, y: Any) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Performs addition of two inputs, validates, persists, and returns result.\"\"\"\n        validated_x = self._validator.validate_int(x)\n        validated_y = self._validator.validate_int(y)\n\n        operation = AddOperation(validated_x, validated_y)\n        result = operation.compute()\n\n        model = OperationModel(\n            id=None,\n            timestamp=iso_timestamp(),\n            x=validated_x,\n            y=validated_y,\n            result=result,\n        )\n        try:\n            self._repo.save(model)\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            logger.warning(f\"Failed to persist operation {model}: {e}\")\n        return result\n\n    def get_history(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[OperationModel]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of recent operations from history.\"\"\"\n        return self._repo.list(limit)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/history_repository.py\n\"\"\"Persistence adapter for SQLite operation history.\"\"\"\n\nimport sqlite3\nimport os\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .models import OperationModel\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\n\nclass HistoryRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages persistence of operation history in a SQLite database.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the repository with the database path.\"\"\"\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._ensure_data_dir()\n        self._ensure_schema()\n\n    def _get_connection(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"Establishes and returns a new database connection.\"\"\"\n        return sqlite3.connect(self._db_path)\n\n    def _ensure_data_dir(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the directory for the SQLite database exists.\"\"\"\n        data_dir = os.path.dirname(self._db_path)\n        if data_dir and not os.path.exists(data_dir):\n            os.makedirs(data_dir)\n\n    def _ensure_schema(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Creates the operations table if it does not already exist.\"\"\"\n        with self._get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS operations (\n                    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                    timestamp TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    x INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                    y INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                    result INTEGER NOT NULL\n                )\n                \"\"\"\n            )\n            conn.commit()\n\n    def save(self, op: OperationModel) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Inserts a new operation into the database.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            with self._get_connection() as conn:\n                cursor = conn.cursor()\n                cursor.execute(\n                    \"INSERT INTO operations (timestamp, x, y, result) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                    (op.timestamp, op.x, op.y, op.result),\n                )\n                conn.commit()\n                return cursor.lastrowid\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to save operation: {e}\") from e\n\n    def list(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[OperationModel]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of recent operations from the database.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            with self._get_connection() as conn:\n                cursor = conn.cursor()\n                cursor.execute(\n                    \"SELECT id, timestamp, x, y, result FROM operations ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT ?\",\n                    (limit,),\n                )\n                rows = cursor.fetchall()\n                return [OperationModel(id=r[0], timestamp=r[1], x=r[2], y=r[3], result=r[4]) for r in rows]\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to list operations: {e}\") from e\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/api_controller.py\n\"\"\"HTTP API layer using FastAPI.\"\"\"\n\nimport uvicorn\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .calculator_service import CalculatorService\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .utils import configure_logging\n\nclass AddRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Request model for the add operation.\"\"\"\n    x: int = Field(..., description=\"First integer operand.\")\n    y: int = Field(..., description=\"Second integer operand.\")\n\nclass AddResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Response model for the add operation.\"\"\"\n    result: int = Field(..., description=\"The sum of x and y.\")\n\nclass HistoryResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Response model for retrieving operation history.\"\"\"\n    id: int = Field(..., description=\"Unique ID of the operation.\")\n    timestamp: str = Field(..., description=\"ISO8601 timestamp of the operation.\")\n    x: int = Field(..., description=\"First operand.\")\n    y: int = Field(..., description=\"Second operand.\")\n    result: int = Field(..., description=\"Result of the operation.\")\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Provides FastAPI app with /add and /history endpoints.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: CalculatorService) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the APIController with a CalculatorService instance.\"\"\"\n        self._service = service\n\n    def create_app(self) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"Creates and configures the FastAPI application.\"\"\"\n        app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"Arithmetic API\",\n            description=\"API for basic arithmetic operations and history.\",\n            version=\"0.1.0\",\n        )\n\n        @app.post(\"/add\", response_model=AddResponse, summary=\"Perform addition of two integers\")\n        async def add_endpoint(request: AddRequest) -> AddResponse:\n            \"\"\"Adds two integers and returns their sum, persisting the operation.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                result = self._service.add(request.x, request.y)\n                return AddResponse(result=result)\n            except ValidationError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e))\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Internal server error: \" + str(e))\n            except Exception as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"An unexpected error occurred: \" + str(e))\n\n        @app.get(\"/history\", response_model=List[HistoryResponse], summary=\"Retrieve recent operation history\")\n        async def get_history_endpoint(limit: int = 100) -> List[HistoryResponse]:\n            \"\"\"Retrieves a list of recent arithmetic operations.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                history = self._service.get_history(limit)\n                return [HistoryResponse(**op.to_dict()) for op in history]\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Internal server error: \" + str(e))\n            except Exception as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"An unexpected error occurred: \" + str(e))\n\n        return app\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Entrypoint for running the FastAPI application.\"\"\"\n    configure_logging()\n    from . import calculator_service_instance\n    cfg = Config.from_env()\n    controller = APIController(calculator_service_instance)\n    app = controller.create_app()\n    uvicorn.run(app, host=cfg.api_host, port=cfg.api_port)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/cli.py\n\"\"\"CLI entrypoint for arithmetic operations.\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .calculator_service import CalculatorService\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .config import Config\nfrom .history_repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom .validator import Validator\nfrom .utils import configure_logging\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line interface interactions for arithmetic operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: CalculatorService) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLIController with a CalculatorService.\"\"\"\n        self._service = service\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses arguments, executes the command, and returns an exit code.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"arith-add\",\n            description=\"Perform arithmetic operations.\"\n        )\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n\n        # 'add' command\n        add_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"add\", help=\"Add two integers.\")\n        add_parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=str, help=\"First integer operand.\")\n        add_parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=str, help=\"Second integer operand.\")\n\n        # 'history' command\n        history_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"history\", help=\"Show recent operation history.\")\n        history_parser.add_argument(\"--limit\", type=int, default=10, help=\"Number of recent operations to show.\")\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n\n        if args.command == \"add\":\n            try:\n                result = self._service.add(args.x, args.y)\n                print(result)\n                return 0\n            except ValidationError as e:\n                print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 2 # Exit code 2 for invalid input\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1 # Generic error\n        elif args.command == \"history\":\n            try:\n                history = self._service.get_history(args.limit)\n                for op in history:\n                    print(f\"ID: {op.id}, Time: {op.timestamp}, {op.x} + {op.y} = {op.result}\")\n                return 0\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f\"An error occurred fetching history: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n        return 1\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Entrypoint for the CLI application.\"\"\"\n    configure_logging()\n    # Initialize service components\n    cfg = Config.from_env()\n    repo = HistoryRepository(cfg.db_path)\n    validator = Validator()\n    service = CalculatorService(repo, validator)\n    \n    controller = CLIController(service)\n    sys.exit(controller.run(sys.argv))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n```python\n# src/arithmetic/utils.py\n\"\"\"Utility functions for common tasks like timestamp generation and logging.\"\"\"\n\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport logging\nimport os\n\ndef iso_timestamp() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Returns the current UTC time in ISO8601 format.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='milliseconds')\n\ndef configure_logging(level: str = \"INFO\") -> None:\n    \"\"\"Configures basic logging for the application.\"\"\"\n    log_level = os.getenv(\"ARITH_LOG_LEVEL\", level).upper()\n    logging.basicConfig(\n        level=getattr(logging, log_level),\n        format=\"%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s\",\n        stream=sys.stdout # Use sys.stdout for consistency with CLI output for now\n    )\n    # Silence uvicorn access logs slightly if not in DEBUG\n    if log_level != \"DEBUG\":\n        logging.getLogger(\"uvicorn.access\").setLevel(logging.WARNING)\n```"}
