{"task_id": "HumanEval/56", "solution": "def correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"<\" and \">\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '<':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == '>':\n            balance -= 1\n        # Other characters are ignored as per critical requirements.\n        if balance < 0:\n            return False\n    return balance == 0"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "def monotonic(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return True is list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    >>> monotonic([1, 2, 4, 20])\n    True\n    >>> monotonic([1, 20, 4, 10])\n    False\n    >>> monotonic([4, 1, 0, -10])\n    True\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(len(l) - 1):\n        if l[i] > l[i+1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        if l[i] < l[i+1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n\n    return is_non_decreasing or is_non_increasing"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/58", "solution": "def common(l1: list, l2: list):\n    \"\"\"Return sorted unique common elements for two lists.\n    >>> common([1, 4, 3, 34, 653, 2, 5], [5, 7, 1, 5, 9, 653, 121])\n    [1, 5, 653]\n    >>> common([5, 3, 2, 8], [3, 2])\n    [2, 3]\n\n    \"\"\"\n    s1 = set(l1)\n    s2 = set(l2)\n    return sorted(s1 & s2)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "To implement the software design specification, I will create the full project structure with multiple files, classes, CLI, and API, as detailed in the architectural overview and file structure sections. The `monotonic` function from the original problem statement will be exposed as part of the library's public API in `src/monotonicer/__init__.py`, fulfilling the `FR2` requirement.\n\n```python\n# src/monotonicer/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"Custom exceptions for the monotonicer library.\"\"\"\n\nclass MonotonicError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for monotonicer library errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass InvalidInputError(MonotonicError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when input sequence is invalid or contains incomparable types.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass PersistenceError(MonotonicError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an error occurs during persistence operations.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n# src/monotonicer/dto.py\n\"\"\"Data Transfer Objects for the monotonicer library.\"\"\"\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any\n\n@dataclass\nclass MonotonicResult:\n    \"\"\"DTO for the result of a monotonicity check.\"\"\"\n    result: bool\n    direction: Optional[str]\n    reason: Optional[str]\n    checked_at: datetime\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Converts the result to a dictionary for serialization.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"result\": self.result,\n            \"direction\": self.direction,\n            \"reason\": self.reason,\n            \"checked_at\": self.checked_at.isoformat()\n        }\n\n# src/monotonicer/utils.py\n\"\"\"Small helper functions for the monotonicer library.\"\"\"\nimport json\nfrom typing import List, Any, Union\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef safe_compare(a: Any, b: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Compares two elements, raising InvalidInputError if they are incomparable.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        if a < b: return -1\n        if a > b: return 1\n        return 0\n    except TypeError as e:\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"Incomparable types: {type(a).__name__} vs {type(b).__name__} ({e})\")\n\ndef _coerce(value: str) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"Attempts to coerce string to int/float, otherwise returns string.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        return int(value)\n    except ValueError:\n        try:\n            return float(value)\n        except ValueError:\n            return value\n\ndef parse_sequence(text: str) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Parses a string into a list, supporting JSON and comma-separated values.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(text)\n        if isinstance(parsed, list):\n            return parsed\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        pass # Not JSON, try CSV\n    \n    parts = [p.strip() for p in text.split(\",\") if p.strip() != \"\"]\n    return [_coerce(x) for x in parts]\n\n# src/monotonicer/validator.py\n\"\"\"Input validation and normalization for the monotonicer library.\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Sequence, List, Any, Union\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .utils import safe_compare, parse_sequence\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates and normalizes input sequences.\"\"\"\n    def normalize(self, seq_or_text: Union[str, Sequence[Any]]) -> List[Any]:\n        \"\"\"Normalizes input to a list of comparable items.\"\"\"\n        if isinstance(seq_or_text, str):\n            return parse_sequence(seq_or_text)\n        elif isinstance(seq_or_text, Sequence):\n            return list(seq_or_text)\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a JSON list string, CSV string, or Python sequence.\")\n\n    def validate(self, seq: Sequence[Any]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that sequence elements are pairwise comparable.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(seq, Sequence):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input must be a sequence, got {type(seq).__name__}.\")\n        for i in range(len(seq) - 1):\n            safe_compare(seq[i], seq[i+1]) # Will raise InvalidInputError if types are incomparable\n\n# src/monotonicer/repository.py\n\"\"\"Abstract base class and implementations for persisting MonotonicResult.\"\"\"\nimport abc\nimport json\nimport sqlite3\nimport logging\nimport os\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .dto import MonotonicResult\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass ResultRepository(abc.ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class for a result repository.\"\"\"\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def save(self, result: MonotonicResult, input_text: str = \"\") -> int:\n        \"\"\"Saves a monotonic result and returns its ID.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def list(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[MonotonicResult]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of saved monotonic results.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def clear(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Clears all persisted results.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\nclass SQLiteRepository(ResultRepository):\n    \"\"\"SQLite implementation of ResultRepository.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes with a database file path.\"\"\"\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._ensure_schema()\n\n    def _get_connection(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"Establishes and returns a database connection.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            conn = sqlite3.connect(self._db_path)\n            conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n            return conn\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"SQLite connection error: {e}\")\n\n    def _ensure_schema(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the 'checks' table exists.\"\"\"\n        conn = None\n        try:\n            conn = self._get_connection()\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS checks (\n                    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                    input_text TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    result INTEGER NOT NULL,\n                    direction TEXT,\n                    reason TEXT,\n                    checked_at TEXT NOT NULL\n                )\n            \"\"\")\n            cursor.execute(\"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_checked_at ON checks(checked_at)\")\n            conn.commit()\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Error ensuring SQLite schema: {e}\")\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Error ensuring schema: {e}\")\n        finally:\n            if conn: conn.close()\n\n    def save(self, result: MonotonicResult, input_text: str = \"\") -> int:\n        \"\"\"Saves a monotonic result to the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        conn = None\n        try:\n            conn = self._get_connection()\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO checks (input_text, result, direction, reason, checked_at)\n                VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\n            \"\"\", (input_text, int(result.result), result.direction, result.reason, result.checked_at.isoformat()))\n            conn.commit()\n            return cursor.lastrowid\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Error saving to SQLite: {e}\")\n        finally:\n            if conn: conn.close()\n\n    def list(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[MonotonicResult]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of saved monotonic results from SQLite.\"\"\"\n        conn = None\n        try:\n            conn = self._get_connection()\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT * FROM checks ORDER BY checked_at DESC LIMIT ?\", (limit,))\n            rows = cursor.fetchall()\n            return [\n                MonotonicResult(\n                    result=bool(row[\"result\"]),\n                    direction=row[\"direction\"],\n                    reason=row[\"reason\"],\n                    checked_at=datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"checked_at\"])\n                ) for row in rows\n            ]\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Error listing from SQLite: {e}\")\n        finally:\n            if conn: conn.close()\n\n    def clear(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Clears all persisted results from the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        conn = None\n        try:\n            conn = self._get_connection()\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"DELETE FROM checks\")\n            conn.commit()\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Error clearing SQLite: {e}\")\n        finally:\n            if conn: conn.close()\n\nclass JSONRepository(ResultRepository):\n    \"\"\"JSON file implementation of ResultRepository.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, file_path: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes with a JSON file path.\"\"\"\n        self._file_path = file_path\n        self._ensure_file()\n\n    def _ensure_file(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the JSON file exists and is a valid array.\"\"\"\n        if not os.path.exists(self._file_path):\n            try:\n                with open(self._file_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                    f.write(\"[]\")\n            except IOError as e:\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"Error creating JSON file {self._file_path}: {e}\")\n\n    def _read_data(self) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Reads all data from the JSON file.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            with open(self._file_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                return json.load(f)\n        except (IOError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n            logger.warning(f\"Could not read from JSON file {self._file_path}, starting fresh: {e}\")\n            return []\n\n    def _write_data(self, data: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Writes data to the JSON file using atomic rename.\"\"\"\n        temp_file = self._file_path + \".tmp\"\n        try:\n            with open(temp_file, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                json.dump(data, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n            os.replace(temp_file, self._file_path) # Atomic rename\n        except IOError as e:\n            if os.path.exists(temp_file):\n                os.remove(temp_file)\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Error writing to JSON file {self._file_path}: {e}\")\n\n    def save(self, result: MonotonicResult, input_text: str = \"\") -> int:\n        \"\"\"Saves a monotonic result to the JSON file.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            data = self._read_data()\n            new_record = result.to_dict()\n            new_record[\"input_text\"] = input_text\n            new_record[\"id\"] = (max([r.get(\"id\", 0) for r in data]) + 1) if data else 1\n            data.append(new_record)\n            self._write_data(data)\n            return new_record[\"id\"]\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Error saving to JSON file: {e}\")\n\n    def list(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[MonotonicResult]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of saved monotonic results from the JSON file.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            data = self._read_data()\n            results = []\n            for record in sorted(data, key=lambda x: x[\"checked_at\"], reverse=True)[:limit]:\n                results.append(MonotonicResult(\n                    result=record[\"result\"],\n                    direction=record.get(\"direction\"),\n                    reason=record.get(\"reason\"),\n                    checked_at=datetime.fromisoformat(record[\"checked_at\"])\n                ))\n            return results\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Error listing from JSON file: {e}\")\n\n    def clear(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Clears all persisted results from the JSON file.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            self._write_data([])\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise PersistenceError(f\"Error clearing JSON file: {e}\")\n\n# src/monotonicer/config.py\n\"\"\"Configuration settings for the monotonicer library.\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport logging\n\nPERSISTENCE_ENABLED: bool = os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_PERSIST\", \"0\").lower() == \"1\"\nPERSISTENCE_TYPE: str = os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_PERSIST_TYPE\", \"sqlite\").lower() # 'sqlite' or 'json'\nDB_PATH: str = os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_DB_PATH\", \"monotonic_checks.db\")\nJSON_PATH: str = os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_JSON_PATH\", \"monotonic_checks.json\")\nLOG_LEVEL: str = os.getenv(\"MONOTONIC_LOG_LEVEL\", \"INFO\").upper()\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=getattr(logging, LOG_LEVEL),\n                    format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# src/monotonicer/core.py\n\"\"\"Core logic for determining sequence monotonicity.\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Sequence, Any, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport logging\nfrom .dto import MonotonicResult\nfrom .validator import InputValidator\nfrom .repository import ResultRepository\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, PersistenceError\nfrom .config import PERSISTENCE_ENABLED, PERSISTENCE_TYPE, DB_PATH, JSON_PATH\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass MonotonicChecker:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a sequence is monotonically increasing or decreasing.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repository: Optional[ResultRepository] = None, validator: Optional[InputValidator] = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes with optional repository and validator dependencies.\"\"\"\n        self._validator = validator or InputValidator()\n        self._repository = repository\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_non_decreasing(seq: Sequence[Any]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a sequence is non-decreasing (a[i] <= a[i+1]).\"\"\"\n        return all(seq[i] <= seq[i+1] for i in range(len(seq) - 1))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_non_increasing(seq: Sequence[Any]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a sequence is non-increasing (a[i] >= a[i+1]).\"\"\"\n        return all(seq[i] >= seq[i+1] for i in range(len(seq) - 1))\n\n    def check(self, seq_input: Any) -> MonotonicResult:\n        \"\"\"Validates input, computes monotonicity, and optionally persists the result.\"\"\"\n        original_input_text = str(seq_input)\n        \n        normalized_seq = self._validator.normalize(seq_input)\n        self._validator.validate(normalized_seq)\n\n        if len(normalized_seq) <= 1:\n            result_obj = MonotonicResult(result=True, direction=\"constant\", reason=\"Sequence length <= 1\", checked_at=datetime.utcnow())\n        else:\n            is_inc = self.is_non_decreasing(normalized_seq)\n            is_dec = self.is_non_increasing(normalized_seq)\n\n            is_monotonic = is_inc or is_dec\n            direction: Optional[str] = None\n            reason: Optional[str] = None\n\n            if is_inc and is_dec:\n                direction = \"constant\"\n                reason = \"Sequence is both non-decreasing and non-increasing (all elements equal).\"\n            elif is_inc:\n                direction = \"increasing\"\n                reason = \"Sequence is non-decreasing.\"\n            elif is_dec:\n                direction = \"decreasing\"\n                reason = \"Sequence is non-increasing.\"\n            else:\n                reason = \"Sequence is not monotonic.\"\n\n            result_obj = MonotonicResult(result=is_monotonic, direction=direction, reason=reason, checked_at=datetime.utcnow())\n        \n        if self._repository:\n            try:\n                # Use the original_input_text for persistence, not normalized_seq\n                self._repository.save(result_obj, input_text=original_input_text)\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to persist check result: {e}\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Unexpected error during persistence: {e}\")\n        return result_obj\n\n# src/monotonicer/__init__.py\n\"\"\"Monotonicity checker library public API.\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Sequence, Any, Optional\n\nfrom .core import MonotonicChecker\nfrom .dto import MonotonicResult\nfrom .exceptions import MonotonicError, InvalidInputError, PersistenceError\nfrom .validator import InputValidator\nfrom .repository import ResultRepository, SQLiteRepository, JSONRepository\nfrom .config import PERSISTENCE_ENABLED, PERSISTENCE_TYPE, DB_PATH, JSON_PATH\n\n# Initialize default checker (lazy instantiation for repository)\n_default_checker: Optional[MonotonicChecker] = None\n\ndef _get_default_checker() -> MonotonicChecker:\n    \"\"\"Provides a singleton default checker instance.\"\"\"\n    global _default_checker\n    if _default_checker is None:\n        repository: Optional[ResultRepository] = None\n        if PERSISTENCE_ENABLED:\n            if PERSISTENCE_TYPE == \"sqlite\":\n                repository = SQLiteRepository(DB_PATH)\n            elif PERSISTENCE_TYPE == \"json\":\n                repository = JSONRepository(JSON_PATH)\n            else:\n                import logging\n                logging.warning(f\"Unknown persistence type '{PERSISTENCE_TYPE}'. Persistence disabled.\")\n        _default_checker = MonotonicChecker(repository=repository)\n    return _default_checker\n\ndef monotonic(seq: Sequence[Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n\n    This function provides a simple boolean check for monotonicity.\n    \"\"\"\n    checker = _get_default_checker()\n    result_dto = checker.check(seq)\n    return result_dto.result\n\ndef check_monotonicity(seq: Sequence[Any]) -> MonotonicResult:\n    \"\"\"Performs a detailed monotonicity check and returns a MonotonicResult DTO.\"\"\"\n    checker = _get_default_checker()\n    return checker.check(seq)\n\n# Public exports\n__all__ = [\n    \"monotonic\",\n    \"check_monotonicity\",\n    \"MonotonicChecker\",\n    \"MonotonicResult\",\n    \"InvalidInputError\",\n    \"PersistenceError\",\n    \"MonotonicError\",\n    \"InputValidator\",\n    \"ResultRepository\",\n    \"SQLiteRepository\",\n    \"JSONRepository\",\n]\n\n# src/monotonicer/cli.py\n\"\"\"Command-line interface for the monotonicer library.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .core import MonotonicChecker\nfrom .validator import InputValidator\nfrom .repository import SQLiteRepository, JSONRepository, ResultRepository\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, MonotonicError\nfrom .config import PERSISTENCE_ENABLED, PERSISTENCE_TYPE, DB_PATH, JSON_PATH, LOG_LEVEL\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line argument parsing and execution.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, checker: MonotonicChecker, argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLI controller with a MonotonicChecker instance and optional argv.\"\"\"\n        self._checker = checker\n        self._argv = argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:]\n        self._parser = self._create_parser()\n\n    def _create_parser(self) -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n        \"\"\"Creates the argparse parser for CLI arguments.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"monoto-check\",\n            description=\"Check if a sequence of elements is monotonically increasing or decreasing.\"\n        )\n        group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n        group.add_argument(\n            \"--list\", \"-l\",\n            help=\"Comma-separated values (e.g., '1,2,3') or JSON array (e.g., '[1,2,3]') input sequence.\"\n        )\n        group.add_argument(\n            \"--file\", \"-f\",\n            help=\"Path to a file containing a JSON array or comma-separated values.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--json\", \"-j\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Output result in JSON format.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--history\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Show the last 100 entries from the persistence history.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--clear-history\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Clear all persistence history.\"\n        )\n        return parser\n\n    def _get_repository(self) -> Optional[ResultRepository]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the configured repository instance, if persistence is enabled.\"\"\"\n        if not PERSISTENCE_ENABLED:\n            logger.debug(\"Persistence is not enabled.\")\n            return None\n        if PERSISTENCE_TYPE == \"sqlite\":\n            return SQLiteRepository(DB_PATH)\n        elif PERSISTENCE_TYPE == \"json\":\n            return JSONRepository(JSON_PATH)\n        else:\n            logger.error(f\"Unknown persistence type '{PERSISTENCE_TYPE}'. Cannot access history.\")\n            return None\n\n    def run(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the CLI command based on parsed arguments.\"\"\"\n        args = self._parser.parse_args(self._argv)\n\n        if args.clear_history:\n            repo = self._get_repository()\n            if repo:\n                try:\n                    repo.clear()\n                    print(\"History cleared successfully.\")\n                    return 0\n                except MonotonicError as e:\n                    print(f\"Error clearing history: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                    return 1\n            else:\n                print(\"Persistence not enabled or configured, cannot clear history.\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n\n        if args.history:\n            repo = self._get_repository()\n            if repo:\n                try:\n                    history = repo.list(limit=100)\n                    if args.json:\n                        print(json.dumps([h.to_dict() for h in history], indent=2))\n                    else:\n                        print(\"--- Monotonicity Check History ---\")\n                        if not history:\n                            print(\"No history records found.\")\n                        for entry in history:\n                            print(f\"[{entry.checked_at.isoformat()}] Result: {entry.result}, Direction: {entry.direction}, Reason: {entry.reason}\")\n                    return 0\n                except MonotonicError as e:\n                    print(f\"Error retrieving history: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                    return 1\n            else:\n                print(\"Persistence not enabled or configured, cannot show history.\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n\n        input_sequence: Optional[str] = None\n        if args.list:\n            input_sequence = args.list\n        elif args.file:\n            try:\n                with open(args.file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                    input_sequence = f.read()\n            except IOError as e:\n                print(f\"Error reading file '{args.file}': {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n                return 1\n\n        if not input_sequence:\n            print(\"No input sequence provided.\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n\n        try:\n            result_dto = self._checker.check(input_sequence)\n            output = result_dto.to_dict()\n\n            if args.json:\n                print(json.dumps(output, indent=2))\n            else:\n                print(f\"Result: {output['result']}\")\n                if output['direction']:\n                    print(f\"Direction: {output['direction']}\")\n                if output['reason']:\n                    print(f\"Reason: {output['reason']}\")\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Invalid input: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except MonotonicError as e:\n            print(f\"An internal error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred.\")\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Main entry point for the CLI tool.\"\"\"\n    repository: Optional[ResultRepository] = None\n    if PERSISTENCE_ENABLED:\n        if PERSISTENCE_TYPE == \"sqlite\":\n            repository = SQLiteRepository(DB_PATH)\n        elif PERSISTENCE_TYPE == \"json\":\n            repository = JSONRepository(JSON_PATH)\n        else:\n            logger.error(f\"Unknown persistence type '{PERSISTENCE_TYPE}'. Persistence disabled.\")\n            repository = None # Ensure it's None if type is invalid\n\n    checker = MonotonicChecker(repository=repository, validator=InputValidator())\n    controller = CLIController(checker, argv)\n    return controller.run()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n\n# src/monotonicer/api.py\n\"\"\"FastAPI application for the monotonicer HTTP API.\"\"\"\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Any, Optional\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Request, Response\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nfrom .core import MonotonicChecker\nfrom .validator import InputValidator\nfrom .repository import SQLiteRepository, JSONRepository, ResultRepository\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, MonotonicError\nfrom .config import PERSISTENCE_ENABLED, PERSISTENCE_TYPE, DB_PATH, JSON_PATH, LOG_LEVEL\nfrom .dto import MonotonicResult\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass SequencePayload(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Pydantic model for the sequence input payload.\"\"\"\n    sequence: List[Any] = Field(..., description=\"The sequence of comparable elements to check.\")\n\ndef get_checker_instance() -> MonotonicChecker:\n    \"\"\"Helper to get a configured MonotonicChecker instance.\"\"\"\n    repository: Optional[ResultRepository] = None\n    if PERSISTENCE_ENABLED:\n        if PERSISTENCE_TYPE == \"sqlite\":\n            repository = SQLiteRepository(DB_PATH)\n        elif PERSISTENCE_TYPE == \"json\":\n            repository = JSONRepository(JSON_PATH)\n        else:\n            logger.error(f\"Unknown persistence type '{PERSISTENCE_TYPE}'. Persistence disabled.\")\n            repository = None # Ensure it's None if type is invalid\n    return MonotonicChecker(repository=repository, validator=InputValidator())\n\n_global_checker = get_checker_instance() # Singleton checker instance for the API\n\ndef create_app(checker: Optional[MonotonicChecker] = None) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"Creates and configures the FastAPI application.\"\"\"\n    app = FastAPI(\n        title=\"Monotonicity Checker API\",\n        description=\"API to determine if a sequence of elements is monotonically increasing or decreasing.\",\n        version=\"0.1.0\",\n    )\n    \n    # Use the global checker by default, or an injected one for testing\n    current_checker = checker or _global_checker\n\n    @app.middleware(\"http\")\n    async def log_requests(request: Request, call_next):\n        \"\"\"Logs incoming HTTP requests.\"\"\"\n        logger.info(f\"Incoming request: {request.method} {request.url}\")\n        response = await call_next(request)\n        logger.info(f\"Outgoing response: {request.method} {request.url} Status: {response.status_code}\")\n        return response\n\n    @app.post(\"/monotonic\", response_model=MonotonicResult)\n    async def check_sequence(payload: SequencePayload):\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if the provided sequence is monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n        \n        Accepts a JSON payload with a 'sequence' field (list of comparable elements).\n        Returns a JSON object with the result, direction, reason, and timestamp.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            result_dto = current_checker.check(payload.sequence)\n            return result_dto\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            logger.warning(f\"Bad Request: {e}\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=str(e))\n        except MonotonicError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Internal MonotonicError: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"An internal processing error occurred.\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred in /monotonic endpoint.\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"An unexpected internal server error occurred.\")\n\n    @app.get(\"/history\", response_model=List[MonotonicResult])\n    async def get_history(limit: int = 100):\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieves the history of monotonicity checks.\n        \n        Returns a list of MonotonicResult objects from the persistence layer.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not PERSISTENCE_ENABLED or not current_checker._repository:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail=\"Persistence is not enabled or configured.\")\n        try:\n            history = current_checker._repository.list(limit=limit)\n            return history\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Persistence error getting history: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Failed to retrieve history from persistence.\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred in /history endpoint.\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"An unexpected internal server error occurred.\")\n\n    @app.post(\"/clear-history\", status_code=204)\n    async def clear_history():\n        \"\"\"\n        Clears all stored history of monotonicity checks.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not PERSISTENCE_ENABLED or not current_checker._repository:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail=\"Persistence is not enabled or configured.\")\n        try:\n            current_checker._repository.clear()\n            return Response(status_code=204)\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Persistence error clearing history: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Failed to clear history from persistence.\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(\"An unexpected error occurred in /clear-history endpoint.\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"An unexpected internal server error occurred.\")\n\n    return app\n\n# Example usage for development (run with `uvicorn monotonicer.api:app --reload`)\napp = create_app()\n\n# pyproject.toml\n\"\"\"Poetry configuration for the monotonicer project.\"\"\"\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"monotonicer\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python library and service to check for monotonicity in sequences.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"monotonicer\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.9,<4.0\"\nfastapi = {version = \"^0.111.0\", optional = true}\nuvicorn = {version = \"^0.30.1\", optional = true}\npydantic = \"^2.0\" # Required by FastAPI\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.0.0\"\nruff = \"^0.3.0\" # For linting and formatting\n\n[tool.poetry.extras]\napi = [\"fastapi\", \"uvicorn\"]\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nmonoto-check = \"monotonicer.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n# README.md\n\"\"\"\n# Monotonicer: Monotonic Sequence Checker\n\nMonotonicer is a Python library and service designed to determine if a sequence (list) of comparable elements is monotonically increasing or decreasing. It provides a flexible API for programmatic use, a command-line interface for quick checks, and an optional HTTP API for remote checks, along with local persistence for auditing.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Core Logic:** Efficient O(n) algorithm to check for non-decreasing or non-increasing sequences.\n- **Library API:** Simple `monotonic()` function for quick boolean checks and `check_monotonicity()` for detailed results.\n- **CLI Tool:** `monoto-check` command-line utility for interactive use.\n- **HTTP API:** FastAPI-based service with a POST endpoint (`/monotonic`) for remote checks and GET/POST for history.\n- **Optional Persistence:** Stores check results in a local SQLite database or JSON file for auditing/debugging.\n- **Robust Error Handling:** Clearly defined exceptions for invalid inputs and persistence issues.\n- **Python 3.9+:** Fully compatible and tested.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install Monotonicer using Poetry or pip:\n\n```bash\n# Using Poetry (recommended for development)\npoetry add monotonicer\npoetry install --with api # Install API dependencies\n\n# Using pip\npip install monotonicer\npip install \"monotonicer[api]\" # Install API dependencies\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library Mode\n\nImport `monotonic` or `check_monotonicity` into your Python projects.\n\n```python\nfrom monotonicer import monotonic, check_monotonicity, InvalidInputError\n\n# Simple boolean check\nprint(monotonic([1, 2, 4, 20]))  # True\nprint(monotonic([1, 20, 4, 10])) # False\nprint(monotonic([4, 1, 0, -10])) # True\nprint(monotonic([5, 5, 5]))      # True\n\n# Detailed result with direction and reason\nresult = check_monotonicity([10, 20, 30])\nprint(f\"Is Monotonic: {result.result}, Direction: {result.direction}, Reason: {result.reason}\")\n# Output: Is Monotonic: True, Direction: increasing, Reason: Sequence is non-decreasing.\n\nresult = check_monotonicity([30, 20, 10])\nprint(f\"Is Monotonic: {result.result}, Direction: {result.direction}, Reason: {result.reason}\")\n# Output: Is Monotonic: True, Direction: decreasing, Reason: Sequence is non-increasing.\n\nresult = check_monotonicity([7, 7, 7])\nprint(f\"Is Monotonic: {result.result}, Direction: {result.direction}, Reason: {result.reason}\")\n# Output: Is Monotonic: True, Direction: constant, Reason: Sequence is both non-decreasing and non-increasing (all elements equal).\n\n# Error handling\ntry:\n    check_monotonicity([1, \"a\", 2]) # Incomparable types\nexcept InvalidInputError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n# Output: Error: Incomparable types: int vs str\n```\n\n### CLI Mode\n\nUse the `monoto-check` command-line tool.\n\n```bash\n# Check a comma-separated list\nmonoto-check --list \"1,2,3,4\"\n# Result: True\n# Direction: increasing\n# Reason: Sequence is non-decreasing.\n\n# Check a JSON list from a string\nmonoto-check -l '[10, 5, 0]' -j\n# {\n#   \"result\": true,\n#   \"direction\": \"decreasing\",\n#   \"reason\": \"Sequence is non-increasing.\",\n#   \"checked_at\": \"...\"\n# }\n\n# Check from a file (e.g., sequence.txt contains \"[1,2,2,3]\")\n# monoto-check --file sequence.txt\n# Result: True\n# Direction: increasing\n# Reason: Sequence is non-decreasing.\n\n# Invalid input\nmonoto-check -l '1,a,2'\n# Invalid input: Incomparable types: int vs str\n\n# View history (if persistence enabled)\n# MONOTONIC_PERSIST=1 monoto-check --history\n# --- Monotonicity Check History ---\n# [...]\n\n# Clear history (if persistence enabled)\n# MONOTONIC_PERSIST=1 monoto-check --clear-history\n# History cleared successfully.\n```\n\n#### CLI Persistence\n\nPersistence is optional and controlled by environment variables:\n- `MONOTONIC_PERSIST=1` to enable persistence.\n- `MONOTONIC_PERSIST_TYPE=sqlite` (default) or `json`.\n- `MONOTONIC_DB_PATH=your_db.db` for SQLite (default: `monotonic_checks.db`).\n- `MONOTONIC_JSON_PATH=your_history.json` for JSON (default: `monotonic_checks.json`).\n\n### HTTP API Mode\n\nTo run the HTTP API service (requires `fastapi` and `uvicorn` installed):\n\n```bash\n# Start the API server\nuvicorn monotonicer.api:app --reload --port 8000\n```\n\nOnce running, you can interact with the API:\n\n**POST /monotonic**\n\n```bash\n# Example using curl\ncurl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/monotonic \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"sequence\": [1, 2, 2, 3]}'\n```\n\nResponse (200 OK):\n```json\n{\n  \"result\": true,\n  \"direction\": \"increasing\",\n  \"reason\": \"Sequence is non-decreasing.\",\n  \"checked_at\": \"2023-10-27T10:00:00.123456\"\n}\n```\n\n**GET /history**\n\nRetrieves recent check history. Persistence must be enabled.\n\n```bash\n# Example using curl\ncurl http://127.0.0.1:8000/history?limit=5\n```\n\nResponse (200 OK):\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"result\": true,\n    \"direction\": \"increasing\",\n    \"reason\": \"Sequence is non-decreasing.\",\n    \"checked_at\": \"...\",\n    \"input_text\": \"[1, 2, 3]\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"result\": false,\n    \"direction\": null,\n    \"reason\": \"Sequence is not monotonic.\",\n    \"checked_at\": \"...\",\n    \"input_text\": \"[1, 5, 2]\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**POST /clear-history**\n\nClears all stored check history. Persistence must be enabled.\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/clear-history\n```\n\nResponse (204 No Content).\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\npytest tests/\n```\n\n### Linting and Formatting\n\n```bash\nruff check src/ tests/\nruff format src/ tests/\n```\n\n## Contributing\n\nContributions are welcome! Please open an issue or submit a pull request.\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License.\n\"\"\"\n\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\n\"\"\"GitHub Actions workflow for continuous integration.\"\"\"\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n      - develop\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n      - develop\n\njobs:\n  build-and-test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n        cache: 'poetry' # Cache poetry dependencies\n\n    - name: Install Poetry\n      run: |\n        pip install poetry\n        poetry self add \"poetry-core<2\" # Fix for older poetry with newer poetry-core\n        poetry config virtualenvs.in-project true\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        poetry install --with api --sync\n\n    - name: Run ruff (linting and formatting check)\n      run: |\n        poetry run ruff check src/ tests/\n        poetry run ruff format src/ tests/ --check\n\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: |\n        poetry run pytest tests/\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/58", "solution": "def common(l1: list, l2: list):\n    \"\"\"Return sorted unique common elements for two lists.\n    Converts inputs to sets for efficient intersection, then sorts the result.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1 = set(l1)\n    set2 = set(l2)\n    common_elements = list(set1.intersection(set2))\n    return sorted(common_elements)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\n# src/lpf/exceptions.py\nclass LPFError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base class for largest prime factor domain errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        return self.message\n\nclass LPFValueError(LPFError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an invalid input value is provided.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n```\n```python\n# src/lpf/models.py\nclass FactorResult:\n    \"\"\"Data model to structure the result of a factoring operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, original: int, largest_factor: int):\n        self.original = original\n        self.largest_factor = largest_factor\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Convert the FactorResult object to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\"original\": self.original, \"largest_factor\": self.largest_factor}\n\n```\n```python\n# src/lpf/utils.py\nimport math\nfrom typing import Iterator\n\nfrom .exceptions import LPFValueError\n\nclass PrimeUtils:\n    \"\"\"Provides low-level numeric helper functions for prime factorization.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def sqrt_floor(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the floor of the square root of n.\"\"\"\n        return math.isqrt(n)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if a number n is prime.\"\"\"\n        if n < 2:\n            raise LPFValueError(\"Input for is_prime must be >= 2\")\n        if n in (2, 3):\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        r = PrimeUtils.sqrt_floor(n)\n        for d in range(3, r + 1, 2):\n            if n % d == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def generate_odd_divisors(limit: int) -> Iterator[int]:\n        \"\"\"Yield odd integers starting from 3 up to a given limit.\"\"\"\n        d = 3\n        while d <= limit:\n            yield d\n            d += 2\n\n```\n```python\n# src/lpf/services.py\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .utils import PrimeUtils\nfrom .exceptions import LPFValueError\nfrom .models import FactorResult # Imported, but not used in current get_largest_prime_factor method implementation, only for 'factorize'\n\nclass FactorService:\n    \"\"\"Implements the business logic for computing the largest prime factor.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, utils: Optional[PrimeUtils] = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the FactorService, optionally with a custom PrimeUtils instance.\"\"\"\n        self._utils = utils or PrimeUtils\n\n    def _validate_input(self, n: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Internal validation for input integer n.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 1:\n            raise LPFValueError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer greater than 1.\")\n\n    def get_largest_prime_factor(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the largest prime factor of n.\"\"\"\n        self._validate_input(n)\n        \n        largest_factor = 1 \n\n        # Remove factors of 2\n        while n % 2 == 0:\n            largest_factor = 2\n            n //= 2\n        \n        # If n became 1, 2 was the largest (e.g., n=8, largest_factor=2)\n        if n == 1:\n            return largest_factor\n\n        # Test odd divisors up to sqrt(n)\n        d = 3\n        while d * d <= n: \n            while n % d == 0:\n                largest_factor = d\n                n //= d\n            d += 2\n        \n        # If n is still greater than 1, the remaining n is prime and is the largest factor.\n        if n > 1:\n            largest_factor = n\n        \n        return largest_factor\n\n    def factorize(self, n: int) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a list of prime factors of n, with multiplicity.\"\"\"\n        self._validate_input(n)\n\n        factors = []\n        \n        # Remove factors of 2\n        while n % 2 == 0:\n            factors.append(2)\n            n //= 2\n        \n        # Test odd divisors up to sqrt(n)\n        d = 3\n        while d * d <= n:\n            while n % d == 0:\n                factors.append(d)\n                n //= d\n            d += 2\n\n        # If n is still greater than 1, the remaining n is prime\n        if n > 1:\n            factors.append(n)\n        \n        return factors\n\n```\n```python\n# src/lpf/controllers.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .services import FactorService\nfrom .exceptions import LPFValueError\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles CLI argument parsing, calls FactorService, and presents results.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: Optional[FactorService] = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLIController, optionally with a custom FactorService.\"\"\"\n        self._service = service or FactorService()\n\n    def _parse_args(self, argv: List[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:\n        \"\"\"Parses command-line arguments.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"lpf-cli\",\n            description=\"Compute the largest prime factor of an integer.\",\n            epilog=\"Example: lpf-cli 13195\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"n\",\n            type=int,\n            help=\"An integer greater than 1 whose largest prime factor will be computed.\"\n        )\n        return parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the CLI logic, returning an exit code.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            args = self._parse_args(argv)\n            result = self._service.get_largest_prime_factor(args.n)\n            print(result)\n            return 0\n        except LPFValueError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n```\n```python\n# src/lpf/cli.py\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Optional, List\n\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\n\nclass MainApp:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the CLI application.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def main(argv: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Main function to run the CLI application.\"\"\"\n        cli_argv = argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:]\n        \n        controller = CLIController() \n        return controller.run(cli_argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(MainApp.main())\n\n```\n```python\n# src/lpf/__init__.py\nfrom .services import FactorService\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Public API wrapper to compute the largest prime factor of n.\n    It delegates the computation to the FactorService.\"\"\"\n    svc = FactorService()\n    return svc.get_largest_prime_factor(n)\n\n```\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"lpf-package\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A Python package to compute the largest prime factor of an integer.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\nlicense = { file = \"LICENSE\" }\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nkeywords = [\"prime-factors\", \"math\", \"cli\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/lpf-package\"\nIssues = \"https://github.com/yourusername/lpf-package/issues\"\n\n[project.dependencies]\n# No external runtime dependencies beyond stdlib as per constraints.\n\n[project.scripts]\nlpf-cli = \"lpf.cli:MainApp.main\"\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=7.0\",\n]\n\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\npythonpath = [\"src\"]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[tool.ruff]\nline-length = 100\ntarget-version = \"py38\"\n\n[tool.ruff.lint]\nselect = [\"E\", \"F\", \"W\", \"C90\", \"I\"]\n\n```\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/python-ci.yml\nname: Python CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [ \"main\" ]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [ \"main\" ]\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.8\", \"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\", \"3.12\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        python -m pip install --upgrade pip\n        pip install \".[dev]\"\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: |\n        pytest\n    - name: Run CLI checks\n      run: |\n        lpf-cli 13195\n        lpf-cli 2048\n        lpf-cli 7\n        ! lpf-cli 1 # Expects exit code 2\n        ! lpf-cli 0 # Expects exit code 2\n        ! lpf-cli -5 # Expects exit code 2\n        ! lpf-cli \"not_an_int\" # Expects exit code 2\n```\n```markdown\n# README.md\n# LPF Package: Largest Prime Factor Calculator\n\nA Python package and CLI tool to compute the largest prime factor of a given integer `n > 1`.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Python API**: `largest_prime_factor(n: int)` for use in other Python code.\n- **CLI Tool**: `lpf-cli <n>` to get the result from the command line.\n- **Robustness**: Handles prime numbers gracefully by returning `n` itself.\n- **Efficiency**: Uses optimized trial division up to `sqrt(n)`.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install the package using pip:\n\n```bash\npip install lpf-package\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Python API\n\n```python\nfrom lpf import largest_prime_factor, LPFValueError\n\n# Example 1: Composite number\nn1 = 13195\nlpf1 = largest_prime_factor(n1)\nprint(f\"The largest prime factor of {n1} is {lpf1}\") # Output: 29\n\n# Example 2: Power of a prime\nn2 = 2048 # 2^11\nlpf2 = largest_prime_factor(n2)\nprint(f\"The largest prime factor of {n2} is {lpf2}\") # Output: 2\n\n# Example 3: A prime number itself\nn3 = 7\nlpf3 = largest_prime_factor(n3)\nprint(f\"The largest prime factor of {n3} is {lpf3}\") # Output: 7\n\n# Example 4: Invalid input\ntry:\n    largest_prime_factor(1)\nexcept LPFValueError as e: \n    print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Output: Error: Input 'n' must be an integer greater than 1.\n```\n\n### CLI Tool\n\n```bash\n$ lpf-cli 13195\n29\n\n$ lpf-cli 2048\n2\n\n$ lpf-cli 7\n7\n\n$ lpf-cli 1\nError: Input 'n' must be an integer greater than 1.\n\n$ lpf-cli --help\nusage: lpf-cli [-h] n\n\nCompute the largest prime factor of an integer.\n\npositional arguments:\n  n           An integer greater than 1 whose largest prime factor will be computed.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n\nExample: lpf-cli 13195\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\nTo run the unit and integration tests, first install the development dependencies:\n\n```bash\npip install \".[dev]\"\npytest\n```\n\n### Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 lpf/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py         # Public API (largest_prime_factor) and package metadata\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py           # Data models (e.g., FactorResult)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py       # Custom exception classes\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py            # Utility functions (e.g., PrimeUtils)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py         # Business logic (FactorService)\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 controllers.py      # CLI logic (CLIController)\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 cli.py              # CLI entry point\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 tests/                      # Unit and integration tests (not provided in this generation)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 .github/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 workflows/\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 python-ci.yml       # GitHub Actions CI configuration\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml              # Project configuration, dependencies, build system\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md                   # Project documentation\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 LICENSE                     # Project license\n```\n```\n# LICENSE\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2023 Your Name\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n```"}
