{"task_id": "HumanEval/73", "solution": "```python\ndef smallest_change(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the minimum number of single-element changes to make an array palindromic.\n    It counts mismatches between symmetric elements from the array's ends inward.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        if arr[i] != arr[-1 - i]:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
