{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "def iscube(a):\n    '''\n    Determines if an integer is a perfect cube.\n    '''\n\n    def _integer_cbrt(val: int) -> int:\n        '''\n        Calculates the integer cube root (floor) of the given integer.\n        '''\n        if val == 0:\n            return 0\n\n        is_negative = val < 0\n        abs_val = abs(val)\n\n        # Estimate the cube root using float power.\n        # This provides a tight initial range for the binary search, ensuring O(1) performance for typical integer sizes.\n        estimate = int(abs_val**(1/3.0))\n\n        # Define the search window for the binary search. A window of +/- 3 is generally robust\n        # against floating-point inaccuracies for common integer ranges.\n        search_low = 0\n        search_high = 0\n\n        if is_negative:\n            # For negative numbers, search for a negative root in a window relative to the estimate.\n            search_low = -(estimate + 3)\n            search_high = -(estimate - 3)\n            if search_low > search_high:  # Ensure low <= high\n                search_low, search_high = search_high, search_low\n            search_low = min(search_low, 0) # Ensure 0 is considered if it falls in the range\n            search_high = max(search_high, 0)\n        else:\n            # For positive numbers, search in a positive window.\n            search_low = max(0, estimate - 3)\n            search_high = estimate + 3\n        \n        # Binary search to find the largest integer 'r' such that r*r*r <= val.\n        # This effectively finds floor(cbrt(val)).\n        result = search_low\n        current_low = search_low\n        current_high = search_high\n\n        while current_low <= current_high:\n            mid = (current_low + current_high) // 2\n            cube_mid = mid * mid * mid\n\n            if cube_mid == val:\n                return mid\n            elif cube_mid < val:\n                result = mid\n                current_low = mid + 1\n            else:  # cube_mid > val\n                current_high = mid - 1\n        return result\n    \n    root = _integer_cbrt(a)\n    return root * root * root == a"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "def iscube(a):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer is a perfect cube using integer arithmetic and binary search.\n    Handles positive, negative, and zero inputs correctly.\n    \"\"\"\n    sign = -1 if a < 0 else 1\n    n = abs(a)\n\n    # Binary search for the integer cube root of n\n    # The upper bound is chosen to be robust against floating point inaccuracies\n    # by adding a small buffer to the initial float estimate of the cube root.\n    lo, hi = 0, max(1, int(n**(1/3)) + 2)\n\n    result_root_abs = 0\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        cube = mid * mid * mid\n        if cube == n:\n            result_root_abs = mid\n            break\n        elif cube < n:\n            result_root_abs = mid  # Store this as a potential floor root\n            lo = mid + 1\n        else:  # cube > n\n            hi = mid - 1\n            \n    # The actual integer cube root, preserving the original sign.\n    final_root = sign * result_root_abs\n    \n    # Check if the cube of this integer root equals the original number.\n    return final_root * final_root * final_root == a"}
