{"task_id": "HumanEval/84", "solution": "```python\ndef solve(N):\n    \"\"\"Given a non-negative integer N, return the total sum of its digits in binary.\n    \n    Example\n        For N = 1000, the sum of digits will be 1 the output should be \"1\".\n        For N = 150, the sum of digits will be 6 the output should be \"110\".\n        For N = 147, the sum of digits will be 12 the output should be \"1100\".\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    total_sum_of_digits = 0\n    # Calculate the sum of decimal digits of N.\n    # This loop correctly computes the sum for all valid N, including N=0.\n    current_N = N\n    while current_N:\n        total_sum_of_digits += current_N % 10\n        current_N //= 10\n    \n    # Convert the sum to a canonical binary string.\n    # Python's bin() handles integer-to-binary conversion, including for 0.\n    return bin(total_sum_of_digits)[2:]\n```"}
