{"task_id": "HumanEval/90", "solution": "```\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"second-smallest-app\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A library and microservice to find the 2nd smallest integer in a list.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"second_smallest_app\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.8.1,<4.0\"\nFlask = \"^2.3.2\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^7.4.0\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nsecond-smallest-cli = \"second_smallest_app.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n```\n# README.md\n# Second Smallest App\n\nThis project provides a library, a command-line interface (CLI), and an HTTP API to compute the second smallest integer in a list.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install the library using pip:\n\n```bash\npip install second-smallest-app\n```\n\nOr, if you prefer poetry:\n\n```bash\npoetry install\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### As a Library\n\n```python\nfrom second_smallest_app.factory import AppFactory\n\n# Get the core service\nfactory = AppFactory()\nservice = factory.create_service()\n\n# Compute the second smallest\nnumbers = [5, 1, 4, 3, 2]\nresult = service.find_second_smallest(numbers)\nprint(f\"The second smallest is: {result}\") # Output: The second smallest is: 2\n\nnumbers_no_distinct_second = [1, 1, 2]\nresult_no_distinct = service.find_second_smallest(numbers_no_distinct_second)\nprint(f\"Result for [1,1,2]: {result_no_distinct}\") # Output: Result for [1,1,2]: 2\n\nnumbers_all_same = [7, 7, 7]\nresult_all_same = service.find_second_smallest(numbers_all_same)\nprint(f\"Result for [7,7,7]: {result_all_same}\") # Output: Result for [7,7,7]: None\n\n```\n\n### CLI\n\nThe CLI tool can accept space-separated integers or a JSON array.\n\n**Space-separated integers:**\n```bash\nsecond-smallest-cli 5 1 4 3 2\n# Output: 2\n\nsecond-smallest-cli 1 1 2\n# Output: 2\n\nsecond-smallest-cli 7 7 7\n# Output: None\n\nsecond-smallest-cli 1\n# Output: None\n\nsecond-smallest-cli\n# Output: Usage: ...\n#         second-smallest-cli: error: the following arguments are required: numbers\n#         or provide --json\n\nsecond-smallest-cli 1 foo 3\n# Output: Error: Invalid input: Element at index 1 is not an integer\n\n```\n\n**JSON array:**\n```bash\nsecond-smallest-cli --json '[5, 1, 4, 3, 2]'\n# Output: 2\n\nsecond-smallest-cli --json '[]'\n# Output: None\n\nsecond-smallest-cli --json '{\"numbers\": [1,2,3]}'\n# Output: Error: Invalid input: Input is not a JSON list.\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nThe API exposes a POST endpoint `/next-smallest`.\n\n**Run the API (development server):**\n```bash\nexport FLASK_APP=src/second_smallest_app/factory.py:create_flask_app\nflask run\n```\n\nOr, using `poetry run`:\n```bash\npoetry run flask --app src/second_smallest_app/factory:create_flask_app run\n```\n\nThe server will start, typically on `http://127.0.0.1:5000`.\n\n**Example request using `curl`:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"numbers\": [5, 1, 4, 3, 2]}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/next-smallest\n# Output: {\"result\":2}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"numbers\": [1, 1, 2]}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/next-smallest\n# Output: {\"result\":2}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"numbers\": [7, 7, 7]}' http://127.00.0.1:5000/next-smallest\n# Output: {\"result\":null}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"numbers\": [\"a\", 2]}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/next-smallest\n# Output: {\"error\":\"Invalid input: Element at index 0 is not an integer\"}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"invalid_key\": [1, 2]}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/next-smallest\n# Output: {\"error\":\"Missing 'numbers' key\"}\n```\n\n## Development\n\nTo set up the development environment:\n\n1. Clone the repository.\n2. Install dependencies: `poetry install`\n3. Run tests: `poetry run pytest`\n```\n```\n# requirements.txt\nFlask==2.3.2\npytest==7.4.0\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/__init__.py\n\"\"\"Package initialization for second_smallest_app.\"\"\"\n\nfrom .factory import AppFactory\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n__all__ = [\"AppFactory\"]\n\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"Domain-specific exceptions for the second smallest app.\"\"\"\n\nclass ValidationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for validation errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass InvalidListError(ValidationError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid list inputs.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, details: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(f\"Invalid input: {details}\")\n        self.details = details\n\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/utils.py\n\"\"\"Small helper functions for parsing and formatting.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nclass Utils:\n    \"\"\"Utility class for common parsing and formatting tasks.\"\"\"\n    JSON_KEY = \"numbers\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def parse_space_separated(s: str) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Parses a space-separated string of integers into a list.\"\"\"\n        if not s.strip():\n            return []\n        try:\n            return [int(x) for x in s.split()]\n        except ValueError as e:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Could not parse space-separated integers: {e}\") from e\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def parse_json_list(s: str) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Parses a JSON array string into a list of integers.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            data = json.loads(s)\n            if not isinstance(data, list):\n                raise ValueError(\"Input is not a JSON list.\")\n            return data\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid JSON format: {e}\") from e\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Error parsing JSON list: {e}\") from e\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def format_result(result: Optional[int]) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Formats the result (an int or None) into a string.\"\"\"\n        return str(result)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/validators.py\n\"\"\"Module for validating list inputs.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Sequence, Any, List\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidListError\n\nclass ListValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates if an input sequence is a valid list of integers.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, max_length: int = 10_000_000) -> None:\n        self._max_length = max_length\n\n    def validate(self, numbers: Sequence[Any]) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Validates the input sequence, ensuring it's a list of integers within size limits.\"\"\"\n        if numbers is None:\n            raise InvalidListError(\"Input is None\")\n        if not hasattr(numbers, \"__iter__\"):\n            raise InvalidListError(\"Input must be an iterable\")\n\n        nums_list = list(numbers)  # Convert to list for consistent length checking and iteration\n        if len(nums_list) > self._max_length:\n            raise InvalidListError(\"Input exceeds maximum allowed length\")\n\n        result: List[int] = []\n        for i, x in enumerate(nums_list):\n            if not isinstance(x, int):\n                raise InvalidListError(f\"Element at index {i} is not an integer\")\n            result.append(x)\n        return result\n\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/services.py\n\"\"\"Core service for computing the second smallest integer.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Sequence, Optional, Tuple\nfrom .validators import ListValidator\n\nclass NextSmallestService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates validation and computes the second smallest element.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, validator: ListValidator) -> None:\n        self._validator = validator\n\n    def find_second_smallest(self, numbers: Sequence[int]) -> Optional[int]:\n        \"\"\"Finds the second smallest element after validating the input list.\"\"\"\n        validated_numbers = self._validator.validate(numbers)\n        min1, min2 = self._compute_two_min(validated_numbers)\n        return min2\n\n    def _compute_two_min(self, numbers: Sequence[int]) -> Tuple[Optional[int], Optional[int]]:\n        \"\"\"Computes the smallest and second smallest elements in a single pass.\"\"\"\n        min1: Optional[int] = None\n        min2: Optional[int] = None\n\n        for n in numbers:\n            if min1 is None or n < min1:\n                # New smallest found, existing min1 becomes second smallest\n                if min1 is not None and n != min1:\n                    min2 = min1\n                elif min1 is not None and n == min1:\n                    # If new smallest is same as current smallest, min2 remains unchanged\n                    pass # Or potentially update if min2 was previously min1, but now min1 is n\n                min1 = n\n            elif n != min1 and (min2 is None or n < min2):\n                # Found a new second smallest, distinct from min1\n                min2 = n\n        return min1, min2\n\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/controllers.py\n\"\"\"CLI controller for processing command-line requests.\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Sequence, List\nfrom .services import NextSmallestService\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom .utils import Utils\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles CLI arguments, calls the service, and prints results or errors.\"\"\"\n    EXIT_OK = 0\n    EXIT_ERROR = 2\n\n    def __init__(self, service: NextSmallestService) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n\n    def run(self, args: Sequence[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses CLI arguments, computes, and prints the result or error message.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Finds the second smallest integer in a list.\",\n            formatter_class=argparse.RawTextHelpFormatter\n        )\n        group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)\n        group.add_argument(\n            \"numbers\",\n            nargs=\"*\",\n            help=\"Space-separated integers (e.g., '1 5 2 8').\"\n        )\n        group.add_argument(\n            \"--json\",\n            dest=\"json_list_str\",\n            help=\"A JSON array string (e.g., '[1, 5, 2, 8]').\"\n        )\n\n        try:\n            parsed_args = parser.parse_args(args)\n            input_list: List[int]\n\n            if parsed_args.json_list_str:\n                input_list = Utils.parse_json_list(parsed_args.json_list_str)\n            else:\n                input_list = [int(x) for x in parsed_args.numbers]\n\n            result = self._service.find_second_smallest(input_list)\n            print(Utils.format_result(result))\n            return self.EXIT_OK\n        except (ValueError, ValidationError) as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return self.EXIT_ERROR\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return self.EXIT_ERROR\n\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/api.py\n\"\"\"Flask-based API controller for HTTP requests.\"\"\"\n\nfrom flask import Flask, request, jsonify\nfrom typing import Tuple, Any\nfrom .services import NextSmallestService\nfrom .utils import Utils\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles HTTP requests and serves the /next-smallest endpoint.\"\"\"\n    ENDPOINT = \"/next-smallest\"\n\n    def __init__(self, service: NextSmallestService) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n\n    def create_app(self) -> Flask:\n        \"\"\"Creates and configures a Flask application with the /next-smallest route.\"\"\"\n        app = Flask(__name__)\n\n        @app.route(self.ENDPOINT, methods=[\"POST\"])\n        def next_smallest_route() -> Tuple[Any, int]:\n            \"\"\"Handles POST requests to /next-smallest to find the second smallest number.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                data = request.get_json()\n                if not data:\n                    return jsonify({\"error\": \"Request must be JSON\"}), 400\n                if Utils.JSON_KEY not in data:\n                    return jsonify({\"error\": f\"Missing '{Utils.JSON_KEY}' key in JSON payload\"}), 400\n\n                numbers = data[Utils.JSON_KEY]\n                result = self._service.find_second_smallest(numbers)\n                return jsonify({\"result\": result}), 200\n            except ValidationError as e:\n                # Specific validation errors from service/validator\n                return jsonify({\"error\": str(e)}), 400\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Catch general errors (e.g., malformed JSON, unexpected issues)\n                app.logger.error(f\"Internal server error: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n                return jsonify({\"error\": \"Internal server error\"}), 500\n        return app\n\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/factory.py\n\"\"\"Application factory for composing services and controllers.\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from flask import Flask\n\nfrom .services import NextSmallestService\nfrom .validators import ListValidator\nfrom .controllers import CLIController\nfrom .api import APIController\n\nclass AppFactory:\n    \"\"\"Central factory for creating and wiring application components.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_LOG_LEVEL = \"INFO\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        # Configure basic logging\n        logging.basicConfig(level=self.DEFAULT_LOG_LEVEL, format='%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n\n    def create_validator(self) -> ListValidator:\n        \"\"\"Creates an instance of ListValidator.\"\"\"\n        return ListValidator()\n\n    def create_service(self) -> NextSmallestService:\n        \"\"\"Creates an instance of NextSmallestService with its dependencies.\"\"\"\n        validator = self.create_validator()\n        return NextSmallestService(validator=validator)\n\n    def create_cli_controller(self) -> CLIController:\n        \"\"\"Creates an instance of CLIController with its dependencies.\"\"\"\n        service = self.create_service()\n        return CLIController(service=service)\n\n    def create_api_controller(self) -> APIController:\n        \"\"\"Creates an instance of APIController with its dependencies.\"\"\"\n        service = self.create_service()\n        return APIController(service=service)\n\n    def create_flask_app(self) -> \"Flask\":\n        \"\"\"Creates and returns a configured Flask application.\"\"\"\n        api_controller = self.create_api_controller()\n        return api_controller.create_app()\n\n```\n```python\n# src/second_smallest_app/cli.py\n\"\"\"Entrypoint for the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Sequence\nfrom .factory import AppFactory\n\ndef main(argv: Sequence[str] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Main function for the CLI application.\"\"\"\n    argv = argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:]\n    factory = AppFactory()\n    controller = factory.create_cli_controller()\n    return controller.run(argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n\n```\n```\n# tests/__init__.py\n```\n```\n# tests/test_api.py\n```\n```\n# tests/test_cli.py\n```\n```\n# tests/test_services.py\n```\n```\n# tests/test_validators.py\n```\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/python-ci.yml\nname: Python CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [ \"main\" ]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [ \"main\" ]\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Set up Python 3.9\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v3\n      with:\n        python-version: \"3.9\"\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        python -m pip install --upgrade pip\n      