{"task_id": "HumanEval/93", "solution": "def encode(message):\n    \"\"\"\n    Write a function that takes a message and encodes it by swapping case of all letters.\n    It also replaces all vowels with the letter two positions ahead in the English alphabet.\n    \"\"\"\n    VOWEL_MAP_LOWER = {'a': 'c', 'e': 'g', 'i': 'k', 'o': 'q', 'u': 'w'}\n    VOWEL_MAP_UPPER = {k.upper(): v.upper() for k, v in VOWEL_MAP_LOWER.items()}\n\n    vowel_mapped_chars = []\n    for char in message:\n        if char in VOWEL_MAP_LOWER:\n            vowel_mapped_chars.append(VOWEL_MAP_LOWER[char])\n        elif char in VOWEL_MAP_UPPER:\n            vowel_mapped_chars.append(VOWEL_MAP_UPPER[char])\n        else:\n            vowel_mapped_chars.append(char)\n\n    intermediate_text = \"\".join(vowel_mapped_chars)\n    encoded_text = intermediate_text.swapcase()\n\n    return encoded_text"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/94", "solution": "def _is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime using trial division with optimizations.\"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n    if n == 2 or n == 3:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n\ndef _sum_digits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the sum of the absolute value of digits of an integer.\"\"\"\n    return sum(int(d) for d in str(abs(n)))\n\ndef skjkasdkd(lst):\n    \"\"\"You are given a list of integers.\n    You need to find the largest prime value and return the sum of its digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_prime = None\n\n    for num in lst:\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            if largest_prime is None or num > largest_prime:\n                largest_prime = num\n\n    if largest_prime is None:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        return _sum_digits(largest_prime)"}
