{"task_id": "HumanEval/131", "solution": "def digits(n):\n    \"\"\"Given a positive integer n, return the product of the odd digits.\n    Return 0 if all digits are even.\n    \"\"\"\n    product = 1\n    found_odd = False\n    # Iterate through digits of n from right to left.\n    while n > 0:\n        digit = n % 10\n        if digit % 2 == 1:\n            product *= digit\n            found_odd = True\n        n //= 10\n    \n    # Return 0 if no odd digits were found, otherwise return the product.\n    return product if found_odd else 0"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/132", "solution": "def is_nested(string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a string of square brackets contains a valid subsequence with nesting (depth >= 2).\n    This checks for the existence of indices p1<p2<p3<p4 such that string[p1]='[', string[p2]='[', string[p3]=']', string[p4]=']'.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    open_count = 0\n    second_open_idx = -1\n\n    # Find the index of the second opening bracket '['\n    for i, char in enumerate(string):\n        if char == '[':\n            open_count += 1\n            if open_count == 2:\n                second_open_idx = i\n                break\n    \n    # If fewer than two opening brackets were found, no nesting is possible\n    if second_open_idx == -1:\n        return False\n    \n    # Count closing brackets ']' strictly after the second opening bracket\n    close_count = 0\n    for i in range(second_open_idx + 1, len(string)):\n        if string[i] == ']':\n            close_count += 1\n            # If two or more closing brackets are found, nesting exists\n            if close_count >= 2:\n                return True\n                \n    return False"}
