{"task_id": "HumanEval/132", "solution": "def is_nested(string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string of brackets contains a valid subsequence with at least one nested pair.\n    It identifies nesting when an inner bracket pair is closed while an outer open bracket can also be matched.\n    \"\"\"\n    open_indices_stack = []\n    all_close_indices = []\n    for i, char in enumerate(string):\n        if char == ']':\n            all_close_indices.append(i)\n\n    close_idx_pointer = 0\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(string):\n        if char == '[':\n            open_indices_stack.append(i)\n        elif char == ']':\n            if open_indices_stack:\n                open_indices_stack.pop()\n                if open_indices_stack:\n                    # An outer open bracket still exists on the stack.\n                    # Check if there's any closing bracket after the current one to form an outer pair.\n                    while close_idx_pointer < len(all_close_indices) and \\\n                          all_close_indices[close_idx_pointer] <= i:\n                        close_idx_pointer += 1\n                    if close_idx_pointer < len(all_close_indices):\n                        return True\n                        \n    return False"}
