{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "```\n# pyproject.toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"lastcharchecker\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A small Python library and CLI to check if the last char of a string is an isolated letter.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" }\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/your-username/lastcharchecker\" # Replace with your repo\n\n[project.scripts]\nlastcharchecker = \"lastcharchecker.__main__:run_cli\"\n\n```\n# README.md\n# lastcharchecker\n\nA small Python library and CLI to determine whether the last character of a string is an alphabetical character that is not part of a word (a \"word\" is a group of characters separated by space).\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install lastcharchecker # (Once published)\n# For local development:\n# git clone <your-repo-url>\n# cd lastcharchecker\n# pip install .\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Programmatic API\n\n```python\nfrom lastcharchecker.api import check_if_last_char_is_a_letter\nfrom lastcharchecker.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n# True examples\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\"apple pi e\"))    # True\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\"e\"))             # True\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\"pi \u00f1\"))          # True (Unicode-aware)\n\n# False examples\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\"apple pie\"))     # False\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\"apple pi e \"))   # False\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\"\"))              # False\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\"apple pi 1\"))    # False\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\"apple pi.\"))     # False\nprint(check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(\" \"))             # False\n\n# Error handling\ntry:\n    check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(None)\nexcept InvalidInputError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Output: Error: Input must be a string\n\ntry:\n    check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(123)\nexcept InvalidInputError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Output: Error: Input must be a string\n```\n\n### Command Line Interface (CLI)\n\n```bash\n# Basic usage\nlastcharchecker \"apple pi e\"\n# Output: True \u2014 last character 'e' is an isolated alphabetic character\n\nlastcharchecker \"apple pie\"\n# Output: False \u2014 last character 'e' is part of a word\n\n# Edge cases\nlastcharchecker \"\"\n# Output: False \u2014 input string is empty after trimming\n\nlastcharchecker \"  \"\n# Output: False \u2014 input string is empty after trimming\n\nlastcharchecker \"e\"\n# Output: True \u2014 last character 'e' is an isolated alphabetic character\n\nlastcharchecker \"e \"\n# Output: False \u2014 last character is a space after trimming\n\nlastcharchecker \"pi \u00f1\"\n# Output: True \u2014 last character '\u00f1' is an isolated alphabetic character\n\n# Invalid input (exit code 2)\nlastcharchecker\n# Output: Invalid input: text argument is required.\n# (Note: argparse will show usage error if no argument provided at all,\n# or for an empty string \"\" it will run and return False)\n```\n\n## Development\n\nTo set up a development environment:\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone <your-repo-url>\ncd lastcharchecker\n\n# Create a virtual environment and activate it\npython -m venv venv\nsource venv/bin/activate # On Windows: .\\venv\\Scripts\\activate\n\n# Install in editable mode\npip install -e .\n\n# Run tests\npytest\n```\n\n## Contributing\n\nFeel free to open issues or submit pull requests.\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License. See the [LICENSE](LICENSE) file for details.\n\n```\n# LICENSE\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2023 Your Name\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/__init_docs__.py\nPACKAGE_NAME = \"lastcharchecker\"\nDESCRIPTION = \"A small Python library and CLI to check if the last char of a string is an isolated letter.\"\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nlastcharchecker package.\nProvides functionality to check if the last character of a string is an isolated letter.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .api import check_if_last_char_is_a_letter\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n__all__ = [\"check_if_last_char_is_a_letter\"]\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/__main__.py\n\"\"\"\nCLI entrypoint for the lastcharchecker package.\nAllows running the checker directly using `python -m lastcharchecker`.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .cli import CLIController\n\ndef run_cli(argv: List[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs the command-line interface with the given arguments.\n    Args:\n        argv: A list of command-line arguments (excluding the program name).\n    Returns:\n        An exit code (0 for success, non-zero for errors).\n    \"\"\"\n    controller = CLIController()\n    return controller.parse_and_run(argv)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(run_cli(sys.argv[1:]))\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/api.py\n\"\"\"\nPublic API for the lastcharchecker library.\nProvides a simple function for programmatic access.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .services import AnalyzerService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(txt: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the last non-space character of a string is an alphabetical\n    character that is not part of a word (a \"word\" is separated by space).\n\n    Args:\n        txt: The input string to evaluate.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the last character meets the criteria, False otherwise.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidInputError: If the input `txt` is None or not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    service = AnalyzerService()\n    result = service.analyze(txt)\n    return result.result\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/models.py\n\"\"\"\nData Transfer Objects (DTOs) for input and output data.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass TextPayload:\n    \"\"\"\n    A simple DTO representing input text for analysis.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, text: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes a TextPayload.\n        Args:\n            text: The raw input string.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.text = text\n\nclass AnalysisResult:\n    \"\"\"\n    A DTO representing the result of a text analysis, including a human-readable reason.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, result: bool, reason: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes an AnalysisResult.\n        Args:\n            result: The boolean outcome of the analysis.\n            reason: A short explanatory message for the result.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.result = result\n        self.reason = reason\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nCustom exception definitions for the lastcharchecker library.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised for invalid or unexpected input types or values.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes an InvalidInputError.\n        Args:\n            message: A descriptive error message.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns the string representation of the exception.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self.message\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/utils.py\n\"\"\"\nUtility functions for text manipulation and character classification.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass TextUtils:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides low-level stateless utility operations for text processing.\n    \"\"\"\n    def trim_trailing_spaces(self, txt: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Removes all trailing ASCII space characters (' ') from a string.\n        Args:\n            txt: The input string.\n        Returns:\n            The string with trailing spaces removed.\n        \"\"\"\n        return txt.rstrip(' ')\n\n    def is_alpha(self, ch: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a given character is a single alphabetic character (Unicode-aware).\n        Args:\n            ch: The character to check.\n        Returns:\n            True if `ch` is a single alphabetic character, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        return len(ch) == 1 and ch.isalpha()\n\n    def previous_char(self, txt: str, idx: int) -> Optional[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns the character immediately preceding the given index in a string.\n        Args:\n            txt: The input string.\n            idx: The current index.\n        Returns:\n            The character at `idx - 1`, or None if `idx` is 0.\n        \"\"\"\n        if idx > 0:\n            return txt[idx - 1]\n        return None\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/analyzer.py\n\"\"\"\nCore logic for analyzing text according to the business rules.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .utils import TextUtils\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass TextAnalyzer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements the core algorithm to determine if the last character\n    is an isolated alphabetical character.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, utils: Optional[TextUtils]=None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the TextAnalyzer with an optional TextUtils instance.\n        Args:\n            utils: An instance of TextUtils to use. If None, a default TextUtils will be created.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._utils = utils or TextUtils()\n\n    def is_last_char_is_letter_not_part_of_word(self, txt: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if the last non-space character of a string is an alphabetical\n        character and is not part of a word.\n\n        Args:\n            txt: The input string (expected to be a string).\n\n        Returns:\n            True if the criteria are met, False otherwise.\n\n        Raises:\n            TypeError: If `txt` is not a string. This is a defensive check;\n                       higher layers are expected to validate input types.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(txt, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'txt' must be a string.\")\n\n        trimmed = self._utils.trim_trailing_spaces(txt)\n\n        if not trimmed:\n            return False\n\n        last_idx = len(trimmed) - 1\n        last_char = trimmed[last_idx]\n\n        if not self._utils.is_alpha(last_char):\n            return False\n\n        if last_idx == 0:\n            # Single character and it's alphabetic -> isolated\n            return True\n\n        # Check the character preceding the last one\n        prev_char = self._utils.previous_char(trimmed, last_idx)\n        return prev_char == ' '\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/services.py\n\"\"\"\nService layer encapsulating business logic and orchestrating analysis.\nHandles input validation and produces structured results.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nfrom .analyzer import TextAnalyzer\nfrom .models import AnalysisResult\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .utils import TextUtils # Needed for reason string detail\n\nclass AnalyzerService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates the analysis process, validates input, and constructs\n    human-readable analysis results.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, analyzer: Optional[TextAnalyzer]=None) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the AnalyzerService with an optional TextAnalyzer instance.\n        Args:\n            analyzer: An instance of TextAnalyzer to use. If None, a default TextAnalyzer will be created.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._analyzer = analyzer or TextAnalyzer()\n        self._utils = TextUtils() # AnalyzerService needs TextUtils for reason string context\n\n    def analyze(self, text: str) -> AnalysisResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Analyzes the given text to determine if its last non-space character\n        is an isolated alphabetical character.\n\n        Args:\n            text: The input string to be analyzed.\n\n        Returns:\n            An AnalysisResult object containing the boolean outcome and a reason string.\n\n        Raises:\n            InvalidInputError: If `text` is None or not a string.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(text, str):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a string\")\n\n        trimmed = self._utils.trim_trailing_spaces(text)\n        \n        # Build reason based on early exit conditions or the analyzer's result\n        reason_template = \"False: last character is not an isolated alphabetic character.\"\n        result_flag = False\n\n        if not trimmed:\n            reason_template = \"False: input string is empty after trimming.\"\n        else:\n            last_idx = len(trimmed) - 1\n            last_char = trimmed[last_idx]\n\n            if not self._utils.is_alpha(last_char):\n                reason_template = f\"False: last character '{last_char}' is not alphabetic.\"\n            elif last_idx > 0 and self._utils.previous_char(trimmed, last_idx) != ' ':\n                reason_template = f\"False: last character '{last_char}' is part of a word.\"\n            else:\n                # Delegate to the analyzer for the actual logic, which should match these checks\n                # but might be more robust for complex cases.\n                # In this specific simple case, the checks above largely replicate analyzer's logic.\n                # The point here is that the SERVICE layer forms the full reason.\n                try:\n                    result_flag = self._analyzer.is_last_char_is_letter_not_part_of_word(text)\n                except TypeError:\n                    # Should ideally not happen if above isinstance check is robust\n                    raise InvalidInputError(\"Internal type error during analysis\")\n\n                if result_flag:\n                    reason_template = f\"True: last character '{last_char}' is an isolated alphabetic character.\"\n                else:\n                    # This path is taken if analyzer returns False after initial checks pass.\n                    # This might imply the previous_char check was not sufficient for a comprehensive reason.\n                    # For current logic, it should align with the 'part of a word' reason.\n                    reason_template = f\"False: last character '{last_char}' is part of a word.\" # Fallback for safety.\n\n        # Re-run analyzer if we reached the final decision point, ensuring consistency\n        # and letting the analyzer dictate the ultimate boolean.\n        # This re-evaluation ensures the business rule is exactly from the analyzer.\n        final_result_from_analyzer = self._analyzer.is_last_char_is_letter_not_part_of_word(text)\n        \n        # Construct reason based on the analyzer's exact decision.\n        if not trimmed:\n            reason = \"input string is empty after trimming.\"\n        elif not self._utils.is_alpha(trimmed[-1]):\n            reason = f\"last character '{trimmed[-1]}' is not alphabetic.\"\n        elif len(trimmed) == 1:\n            # Single character and it's alpha, so isolated.\n            reason = f\"last character '{trimmed[-1]}' is an isolated alphabetic character.\"\n        elif trimmed[-2] != ' ':\n            reason = f\"last character '{trimmed[-1]}' is part of a word.\"\n        else: # trimmed[-2] == ' '\n            reason = f\"last character '{trimmed[-1]}' is an isolated alphabetic character.\"\n\n        return AnalysisResult(final_result_from_analyzer, reason)\n\n```\n# src/lastcharchecker/cli.py\n\"\"\"\nCommand-Line Interface (CLI) controller for the lastcharchecker.\nHandles argument parsing, service interaction, and output presentation.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List\n\nfrom .services import AnalyzerService\nfrom .models import AnalysisResult\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom .__init_docs__ import PACKAGE_NAME, DESCRIPTION\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages the command-line interface, including argument parsing,\n    invoking the AnalyzerService, and printing results.\n    \"\"\"\n    def parse_and_run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses command-line arguments and executes the analysis.\n        Args:\n            argv: A list of arguments passed to the CLI (excluding the program name).\n        Returns:\n            An exit code (0 for success, non-zero for errors).\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=PACKAGE_NAME,\n            description=DESCRIPTION,\n            formatter_class=argparse.RawTextHelpFormatter\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"text\",\n            nargs=\"?\",  # Makes the argument optional\n            default=None, # Explicitly default to None to differentiate from empty string\n            help=\"The text string to evaluate. Wrap in quotes if it contains spaces.\"\n        )\n        \n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        if args.text is None:\n            # If no argument was provided at all\n            parser.print_help(sys.stderr)\n            print(\"\\nError: text argument is required.\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n            \n        service = AnalyzerService()\n        try:\n            result = service.analyze(args.text)\n            self._print_result(result)\n            return 0\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Invalid input: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n    def _print_result(self, result: AnalysisResult) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Prints the analysis result to standard output in a user-friendly format.\n        Args:\n            result: The AnalysisResult object to print.\n        \"\"\"\n        print(f\"{result.result} \u2014 {result.reason}\")\n\n```"}
