{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "def Strongest_Extension(class_name, extensions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the strongest extension based on (CAP - SM) and returns \"ClassName.StrongestExtensionName\".\n    Tie-breaks by first appearance in the list if strengths are equal.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _compute_strength_for_extension(ext_name):\n        \"\"\"Calculates strength as count of uppercase minus count of lowercase letters.\"\"\"\n        caps = sum(1 for char in ext_name if char.isupper())\n        sm = sum(1 for char in ext_name if char.islower())\n        return caps - sm\n\n    if not extensions:\n        return class_name\n\n    strongest_extension_name = extensions[0]\n    max_strength = _compute_strength_for_extension(extensions[0])\n\n    for i in range(1, len(extensions)):\n        current_extension = extensions[i]\n        current_strength = _compute_strength_for_extension(current_extension)\n\n        # Tie-break by first appearance: only update if strictly stronger\n        if current_strength > max_strength:\n            max_strength = current_strength\n            strongest_extension_name = current_extension\n\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_extension_name}\""}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/152", "solution": "```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"matchcompare\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A service to compare match scores and guesses.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"matchcompare\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.9,<4.0\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.30.1\"}\npydantic = \"^2.7.3\" # FastAPI dependency\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.2\"\nflake8 = \"^7.1.0\"\nblack = \"^24.4.2\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nmatchcompare = \"matchcompare.cli:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n\n## MatchCompare Service\n\nThis project implements a service for comparing actual match scores against guessed scores, providing both a REST API and a CLI interface.\n\n### Features:\n- **Core Logic**: Computes the absolute difference between each actual score and its corresponding guess.\n- **REST API**: A `POST /compare` endpoint using FastAPI to submit scores and guesses.\n- **CLI Tool**: A `matchcompare compare` command to perform comparisons from the command line, accepting JSON arrays or file paths.\n- **Input Validation**: Ensures inputs are valid integer lists of equal length.\n- **Optional API Key**: The API can be configured with an optional API key for basic security.\n\n### Installation\n\n1.  **Clone the repository**:\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/your-org/matchcompare.git\n    cd matchcompare\n    ```\n\n2.  **Install dependencies using Poetry**:\n    ```bash\n    poetry install\n    ```\n\n### Usage\n\n#### CLI\n\nThe CLI tool allows you to compare scores directly from your terminal.\n\n```bash\n# Using JSON arrays as arguments\nmatchcompare '[1,2,3]' '[1,2,5]'\n# Expected output: {\"result\": [0, 0, 2]}\n\n# Using JSON files (e.g., game.json and guess.json)\n# game.json: [10, 20]\n# guess.json: [12, 18]\nmatchcompare game.json guess.json\n# Expected output: {\"result\": [2, 2]}\n```\n\n#### REST API\n\n1.  **Start the API server**:\n    ```bash\n    poetry run uvicorn src.matchcompare.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n    ```\n    The API will be available at `http://localhost:8000`.\n\n2.  **Make a request**:\n    You can use `curl` or any API client to send a POST request to `/compare`.\n\n    ```bash\n    curl -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/compare\" \\\n         -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n         -d '{\n               \"game\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 1],\n               \"guess\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 2, -2]\n             }'\n    # Expected output: {\"result\": [0,0,0,0,3,3]}\n    ```\n\n3.  **With API Key (if configured)**:\n    If the API is initialized with an API key (e.g., `poetry run uvicorn src.matchcompare.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --app-env API_KEY=\"your_secret_key\"` or by modifying `create_app` in `api.py`), include it in the `X-API-Key` header:\n\n    ```bash\n    curl -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/compare\" \\\n         -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n         -H \"X-API-Key: your_secret_key\" \\\n         -d '{\n               \"game\": [1, 2, 3],\n               \"guess\": [1, 2, 5]\n             }'\n    ```\n\n### Development\n\n#### Running Tests\n\n(Note: Test files are not provided in this generation, but the structure supports them.)\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\n#### Code Formatting and Linting\n\n```bash\npoetry run black src/\npoetry run flake8 src/\n```\n\n### Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 matchcompare/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 controllers.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 api.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 errors.py\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 .github/\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 workflows/\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 ci.yml\n```\n```\n\n```python\n# src/matchcompare/__init__.py\n\"\"\"MatchCompare package init.\"\"\"\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n```\n\n```python\n# src/matchcompare/errors.py\n\"\"\"Custom exceptions for the matchcompare application.\"\"\"\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when input data does not meet validation requirements.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\nclass AuthenticationError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an API key is missing or invalid.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n```\n\n```python\n# src/matchcompare/utils.py\n\"\"\"Utility functions for input validation and coercion.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Sequence, List\nfrom .errors import InvalidInputError\n\ndef ensure_int_list(seq: Sequence) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Ensures input is a list-like sequence of integers, raising InvalidInputError otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(seq, (list, tuple)):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list/array of integers.\")\n    out = []\n    for i, v in enumerate(seq):\n        if not isinstance(v, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"All items must be integers; index {i} is {type(v).__name__}.\")\n        out.append(v)\n    return out\n\ndef validate_equal_length(game: List[int], guess: List[int]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates that two lists have the same length, raising InvalidInputError if not.\"\"\"\n    if len(game) != len(guess):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Game and guess arrays must have the same length.\")\n```\n\n```python\n# src/matchcompare/models.py\n\"\"\"Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) for request and response, with validation.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .utils import ensure_int_list, validate_equal_length\nfrom .errors import InvalidInputError\n\nclass CompareRequestDTO:\n    \"\"\"Represents a comparison request with game scores and guesses.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, game: List[int], guess: List[int]) -> None:\n        self.game = ensure_int_list(game)\n        self.guess = ensure_int_list(guess)\n        self.validate()\n\n    def validate(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates the DTO's internal data, ensuring equal length.\"\"\"\n        validate_equal_length(self.game, self.guess)\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Converts the DTO to a dictionary for serialization.\"\"\"\n        return {\"game\": self.game, \"guess\": self.guess}\n\nclass CompareResponseDTO:\n    \"\"\"Represents a comparison response containing the result list.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, result: List[int]) -> None:\n        self.result = result\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Converts the DTO to a dictionary for serialization.\"\"\"\n        return {\"result\": self.result}\n```\n\n```python\n# src/matchcompare/services.py\n\"\"\"Core business logic for score comparison.\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass ScoreComparator:\n    \"\"\"A stateless service for computing absolute differences between scores.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        pass\n\n    def compare(self, game: List[int], guess: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Computes the per-index absolute differences between two lists of integers.\n        \n        Assumes `game` and `guess` are validated lists of equal length.\n        \"\"\"\n        return [abs(g_score - q_score) for g_score, q_score in zip(game, guess)]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/matchcompare/controllers.py\n\"\"\"Controllers for handling API and CLI requests, orchestrating service calls.\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport json\nfrom typing import Callable, TextIO\nfrom .services import ScoreComparator\nfrom .models import CompareRequestDTO, CompareResponseDTO\nfrom .errors import InvalidInputError\n\n# CLI exit codes\nEXIT_OK = 0\nEXIT_ERROR = 2\n\nclass ApiController:\n    \"\"\"Handles requests from the API, performing validation and delegating to the comparator.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, comparator: ScoreComparator) -> None:\n        self.comparator = comparator\n\n    def process_request(self, payload: dict) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Processes an API request payload, returning a serializable response.\"\"\"\n        game = payload.get(\"game\")\n        guess = payload.get(\"guess\")\n\n        request_dto = CompareRequestDTO(game=game, guess=guess) # Validation happens in DTO constructor\n        result = self.comparator.compare(request_dto.game, request_dto.guess)\n        response_dto = CompareResponseDTO(result=result)\n        return response_dto.to_dict()\n\nclass CliController:\n    \"\"\"Handles requests from the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, comparator: ScoreComparator, out: TextIO = sys.stdout, err: TextIO = sys.stderr) -> None:\n        self.comparator = comparator\n        self.out = out\n        self.err = err\n\n    def _read_json_input(self, arg_value: str) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Tries to parse arg_value as JSON or read from a file path.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            return json.loads(arg_value)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            try:\n                with open(arg_value, 'r') as f:\n                    return json.load(f)\n            except (FileNotFoundError, IOError):\n                raise InvalidInputError(f\"Could not parse '{arg_value}' as JSON or read from file.\")\n\n    def run(self, game_arg: str, guess_arg: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses CLI arguments, computes differences, and prints JSON result to stdout.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            game = self._read_json_input(game_arg)\n            guess = self._read_json_input(guess_arg)\n\n            request_dto = CompareRequestDTO(game=game, guess=guess)\n            result = self.comparator.compare(request_dto.game, request_dto.guess)\n            response_dto = CompareResponseDTO(result=result)\n\n            json.dump(response_dto.to_dict(), self.out)\n            self.out.write(\"\\n\")\n            return EXIT_OK\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            self.err.write(f\"Error: {e}\\n\")\n            return EXIT_ERROR\n        except Exception as e:\n            self.err.write(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\\n\")\n            return EXIT_ERROR\n```\n\n```python\n# src/matchcompare/api.py\n\"\"\"FastAPI application factory and ASGI app instance.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Header, status, Depends\nfrom fastapi.security import APIKeyHeader\nfrom .controllers import ApiController\nfrom .services import ScoreComparator\nfrom .errors import InvalidInputError, AuthenticationError\n\n# Define API key header for FastAPI\napi_key_header = APIKeyHeader(name=\"X-API-Key\", auto_error=False)\n\nasync def get_api_key(api_key_value: Optional[str] = None, x_api_key: str = Depends(api_key_header)) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Dependency to validate the API key from the header.\"\"\"\n    if api_key_value is None:\n        return x_api_key # No API key configured, so any provided key is ignored, or no key is needed.\n\n    if x_api_key is None:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail=\"Missing API key\",\n        )\n    if x_api_key != api_key_value:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_401_UNAUTHORIZED,\n            detail=\"Invalid API key\",\n        )\n    return x_api_key\n\ndef create_app(api_key: Optional[str] = None) -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"Creates and configures the FastAPI application.\"\"\"\n    app = FastAPI(\n        title=\"MatchCompare API\",\n        description=\"API for comparing match scores and guesses.\",\n        version=\"0.1.0\"\n    )\n\n    comparator = ScoreComparator()\n    controller = ApiController(comparator)\n\n    @app.post(\"/compare\", summary=\"Compare actual game scores with guesses\")\n    async def compare_endpoint(payload: dict, authenticated_api_key: str = Depends(lambda k=api_key: get_api_key(k))):\n        \"\"\"\n        Receives game and guess arrays, computes absolute differences.\n        An optional API key can be provided in the 'X-API-Key' header.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            return controller.process_request(payload)\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e))\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"An unexpected error occurred.\")\n\n    return app\n\n# Retrieve API_KEY from environment variable if available for default app instance\n_api_key_from_env = os.getenv(\"API_KEY\")\napp = create_app(api_key=_api_key_from_env)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/matchcompare/cli.py\n\"\"\"Command-line interface entrypoint for matchcompare.\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport os\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom .controllers import CliController\nfrom .services import ScoreComparator\n\ndef main(argv: Optional[list[str]] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Main entry point for the matchcompare CLI.\"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        prog=\"matchcompare\",\n        description=\"Compares actual match scores with guesses.\"\n    )\n    \n    # Subcommand for 'compare' logic\n    subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", help=\"Available commands\", required=True)\n    \n    compare_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n        \"compare\", \n        help=\"Compute differences between game scores and guesses.\"\n    )\n    compare_parser.add_argument(\n        \"game\", \n        help=\"JSON array of actual game scores or path to a JSON file containing the array.\"\n    )\n    compare_parser.add_argument(\n        \"guess\", \n        help=\"JSON array of guessed scores or path to a JSON file containing the array.\"\n    )\n\n    args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n    if args.command == \"compare\":\n        comparator = ScoreComparator()\n        # Pass sys.stdout and sys.stderr to CliController for testability\n        controller = CliController(comparator, out=sys.stdout, err=sys.stderr)\n        return controller.run(args.game, args.guess)\n    \n    return CliController.EXIT_ERROR # Should not be reached with required=True for subparsers\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n```\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: Python CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [ main ]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [ main ]\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\", \"3.12\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n        cache: 'poetry'\n\n    - name: Install Poetry\n      run: pip install poetry\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: poetry install --no-root\n\n    - name: Run Black formatter check\n      run: poetry run black --check src/\n\n    - name: Run Flake8 linter\n      run: poetry run flake8 src/\n\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: poetry run pytest\n      env:\n        API_KEY: \"test_secret_key\" # Provide a dummy API key for API tests\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "def Strongest_Extension(class_name, extensions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the strongest extension based on CAP - SM rule and returns\n    the class name combined with the strongest extension name.\n    Tie-breaking favors the extension that appears first in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    strongest_extension_name = None\n    max_strength = float('-inf')\n\n    for extension_name in extensions:\n        cap_count = 0\n        sm_count = 0\n        for char in extension_name:\n            if char.isupper():\n                cap_count += 1\n            elif char.islower():\n                sm_count += 1\n        \n        current_strength = cap_count - sm_count\n\n        if current_strength > max_strength:\n            max_strength = current_strength\n            strongest_extension_name = extension_name\n        # The tie-breaking rule to choose the first one in the list is\n        # implicitly handled by not updating if current_strength == max_strength.\n\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_extension_name}\""}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/154", "solution": "def cycpattern_check(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Checks if b or any of its rotations is a substring of a.\n    This function handles empty strings for a and b appropriately.\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_rotations = []\n    # Handle empty string b; an empty string is a substring of any string.\n    if not b:\n        unique_rotations = [\"\"]\n    else:\n        seen = set()\n        n = len(b)\n        for i in range(n):\n            rotation = b[i:] + b[:i]\n            if rotation not in seen:\n                unique_rotations.append(rotation)\n                seen.add(rotation)\n\n    for rot in unique_rotations:\n        # Use Python's 'in' operator for efficient substring search.\n        if rot in a:\n            return True\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/155", "solution": "def even_odd_count(num):\n    \"\"\"Given an integer, return a tuple that has the number of even and odd digits respectively.\n    This function counts digits of the absolute value, treating 0 as a single even digit.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = abs(num)\n    if n == 0:\n        return (1, 0)\n\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    while n > 0:\n        digit = n % 10\n        if digit % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n        n //= 10\n\n    return (even_count, odd_count)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/154", "solution": "def cycpattern_check(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Checks if any rotation of pattern 'b' is a substring in text 'a'.\n    This implementation uses the KMP algorithm for substring searching.\"\"\"\n\n    if not b:\n        return False\n\n    if len(b) > len(a):\n        return False\n\n    def _build_lps(pat: str) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Builds the Longest Proper Prefix which is also Suffix array for KMP.\"\"\"\n        lps = [0] * len(pat)\n        length = 0\n        i = 1\n        while i < len(pat):\n            if pat[i] == pat[length]:\n                length += 1\n                lps[i] = length\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                if length:\n                    length = lps[length - 1]\n                else:\n                    lps[i] = 0\n                    i += 1\n        return lps\n\n    def _kmp_matches(text: str, pattern: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Performs KMP substring matching.\"\"\"\n        lt, lp = len(text), len(pattern)\n        lps = _build_lps(pattern)\n        i = j = 0  # i for text, j for pattern\n        while i < lt:\n            if text[i] == pattern[j]:\n                i += 1\n                j += 1\n                if j == lp:  # Pattern found\n                    return True\n            else:\n                if j:  # Mismatch after some characters matched\n                    j = lps[j - 1]\n                else:  # Mismatch at the beginning\n                    i += 1\n        return False\n\n    rotations_set = set()\n    n = len(b)\n    for i in range(n):\n        rotation = b[i:] + b[:i]\n        rotations_set.add(rotation)\n\n    for rotation in rotations_set:\n        if _kmp_matches(a, rotation):\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/156", "solution": "def int_to_mini_roman(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer (1-1000), return its lowercase Roman numeral equivalent.\n    This function assumes valid input as per the problem constraints.\n    \"\"\"\n    roman_map = [\n        (1000, 'M'), (900, 'CM'), (500, 'D'), (400, 'CD'),\n        (100, 'C'), (90, 'XC'), (50, 'L'), (40, 'XL'),\n        (10, 'X'), (9, 'IX'), (5, 'V'), (4, 'IV'),\n        (1, 'I')\n    ]\n\n    result = []\n    n = number\n    for value, symbol in roman_map:\n        while n >= value:\n            result.append(symbol)\n            n -= value\n    return \"\".join(result).lower()"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/155", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"digitstats\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Utility to count even and odd digits in an integer.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"digitstats\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \"^3.10\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.30.1\"}\npydantic = \"^2.7.1\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.1\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\ndigitstats = \"digitstats.cli_entry:main\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n```python\n# requirements.txt\nfastapi>=0.111.0,<0.112.0\nuvicorn[standard]>=0.30.1,<0.31.0\npydantic>=2.7.1,<2.8.0\npytest>=8.2.1,<8.3.0\n```\n```markdown\n# README.md\n\n# DigitStats\n\nA Python utility to count even and odd digits in an integer. Provides a reusable library, a command-line interface (CLI), and an HTTP API.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Core Library**: `digitstats.services.EvenOddCounter` for programmatic use.\n- **CLI**: `digitstats count <number>` to quickly get digit statistics from your terminal.\n- **HTTP API**: `POST /count` endpoint for integration with other services.\n- **History Persistence**: Records all invocations to a local JSON Lines file (`history.jsonl`) by default for diagnostics.\n\n## Installation\n\n1. **Prerequisites**: Python 3.10+\n2. **Install using Poetry (recommended)**:\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repository_url> # Replace with your repository URL\n   cd digitstats\n   poetry install\n   ```\n3. **Install using pip**:\n   ```bash\n   pip install -r requirements.txt\n   pip install -e .\n   ```\n\n## Usage\n\n### CLI\n\nCount digits:\n```bash\ndigitstats count 12345\n# Output: (2, 3)\n\ndigitstats count -100\n# Output: (3, 0)\n\ndigitstats count \"007\" # Leading zeros count as digits\n# Output: (2, 1)\n\ndigitstats count 12345 --json\n# Output: {\"input\": 12345, \"even\": 2, \"odd\": 3, \"timestamp\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmmZ\"}\n```\n\nFor more options:\n```bash\ndigitstats --help\ndigitstats count --help\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nRun the API server (requires `uvicorn`):\n```bash\nuvicorn src.digitstats.adapters.http_app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThen, make a POST request:\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"number\": 12345}' http://localhost:8000/count\n# Response: {\"input\": 12345, \"even\": 2, \"odd\": 3, \"timestamp\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmmZ\"}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"number\": \"-100\"}' http://localhost:8000/count\n# Response: {\"input\": -100, \"even\": 3, \"odd\": 0, \"timestamp\": \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmmZ\"}\n```\n\n### Python Library\n\n```python\nfrom digitstats.services.counter import EvenOddCounter\nfrom digitstats.models import DigitCountResult\n\ncounter = EvenOddCounter()\nresult: DigitCountResult = counter.count(12345)\nprint(f\"Input: {result.input_value}, Even: {result.even}, Odd: {result.odd}\")\n# Output: Input: 12345, Even: 2, Odd: 3\n\nresult_neg: DigitCountResult = counter.count(\"-12\")\nprint(f\"Input: {result_neg.input_value}, Even: {result_neg.even}, Odd: {result_neg.odd}\")\n# Output: Input: -12, Even: 1, Odd: 1\n```\n\n## Development\n\nRun tests:\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\nor\n```bash\npython -m pytest\n```\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/__init__.py\n\"\"\"DigitStats: A utility for counting even and odd digits.\"\"\"\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/models.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass DigitCountResult:\n    \"\"\"Domain model for the result of digit counting, including original input and timestamp.\"\"\"\n    input_value: int\n    even: int\n    odd: int\n    timestamp: datetime\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Converts the result to a dictionary for serialization.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"input\": self.input_value,\n            \"even\": self.even,\n            \"odd\": self.odd,\n            \"timestamp\": self.timestamp.astimezone(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='milliseconds').replace('+00:00', 'Z')\n        }\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_tuple(input_value: int, even: int, odd: int, timestamp: datetime | None = None) -> \"DigitCountResult\":\n        \"\"\"Factory method to create a DigitCountResult from basic counts.\"\"\"\n        return DigitCountResult(input_value, even, odd, timestamp or datetime.now(timezone.utc))\n\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/services/__init__.py\n# Marker file for Python package\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/services/counter.py\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom digitstats.models import DigitCountResult\nfrom digitstats.services.validator import InputValidator\nfrom digitstats.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass EvenOddCounter:\n    \"\"\"Core service for counting even and odd digits in a number.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, validator: InputValidator | None = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the counter with an optional input validator.\"\"\"\n        self.validator = validator or InputValidator()\n\n    def count(self, number: int | str) -> DigitCountResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Counts even and odd digits in the given number.\n        The sign of the number is ignored for counting.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            # Determine the original integer value for the result object.\n            # This handles strings like \"123\", \"-123\", \"  +123  \", \"007\" -> 7\n            original_int_value: int\n            if isinstance(number, int):\n                original_int_value = number\n            else: # isinstance(number, str)\n                original_int_value = int(str(number).strip())\n        except ValueError as e:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Cannot parse original input value '{number}' to an integer: {e}\")\n\n        # Validate and normalize input to a digits-only string (sign removed, whitespace removed)\n        digits_str = self.validator.validate_number(number)\n        \n        even, odd = self._count_digits(digits_str)\n        return DigitCountResult.from_tuple(original_int_value, even, odd, datetime.now(timezone.utc))\n\n    def _count_digits(self, digits: str) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Iterates through a string of digits to count even and odd occurrences.\"\"\"\n        even_count = 0\n        for ch in digits:\n            if int(ch) % 2 == 0:\n                even_count += 1\n        odd_count = len(digits) - even_count\n        return even_count, odd_count\n\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/services/validator.py\nfrom digitstats.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates and normalizes numeric inputs for digit counting.\"\"\"\n\n    def validate_number(self, value: int | str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates if the input represents a valid integer and returns its absolute string representation.\n        Sign is ignored, leading zeros are preserved if part of string input.\n        \"\"\"\n        s = self._strip_sign_and_whitespace(str(value))\n        if not s: # handle empty string after stripping, or just a sign\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input '{value}' is empty or only a sign after stripping.\")\n        if not s.isdigit():\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Input '{value}' contains non-digit characters after stripping sign.\")\n        return s\n\n    def _strip_sign_and_whitespace(self, value: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Helper to strip leading/trailing whitespace and optional leading sign characters.\"\"\"\n        s = value.strip()\n        if s.startswith(('+', '-')):\n            s = s[1:]\n        return s\n\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/repositories/__init__.py\n# Marker file for Python package\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/repositories/history_repo.py\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom threading import Lock\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nfrom digitstats.models import DigitCountResult\nfrom digitstats.utils.logger import logger\n\nclass HistoryRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class for history repositories.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def append(self, record: DigitCountResult) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a new history record.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def list_all(self) -> list[DigitCountResult]:\n        \"\"\"Lists all stored history records.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\nclass InMemoryHistoryRepository(HistoryRepository):\n    \"\"\"An in-memory implementation of HistoryRepository, suitable for testing or ephemeral use.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Initializes an empty in-memory list for records.\"\"\"\n        self._records: list[DigitCountResult] = []\n\n    def append(self, record: DigitCountResult) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a record to the in-memory list.\"\"\"\n        self._records.append(record)\n\n    def list_all(self) -> list[DigitCountResult]:\n        \"\"\"Returns a shallow copy of all in-memory records.\"\"\"\n        return list(self._records)\n\nclass JSONFileHistoryRepository(HistoryRepository):\n    \"\"\"\n    Persists history records to a local JSON Lines file.\n    Each line is a JSON object representing a DigitCountResult.\n    \"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_HISTORY_PATH = Path(\"history.jsonl\")\n\n    def __init__(self, path: Path | str | None = None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the repository with a specified file path.\n        Creates parent directories if they don't exist.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._path = (Path(path) if path else self.DEFAULT_HISTORY_PATH).resolve()\n        self._lock = Lock()\n        self._path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        logger.debug(f\"JSONFileHistoryRepository initialized with path: {self._path}\")\n\n\n    def append(self, record: DigitCountResult) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a new record as a JSON line to the file.\"\"\"\n        line = json.dumps(record.to_dict(), ensure_ascii=False)\n        with self._lock:\n            try:\n                with open(self._path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                    f.write(line + \"\\n\")\n                logger.debug(f\"Appended record to {self._path}: {record.input_value}\")\n            except IOError as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to append history record to {self._path}: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n\n    def list_all(self) -> list[DigitCountResult]:\n        \"\"\"Reads all records from the JSON Lines file and returns them as a list.\"\"\"\n        results = []\n        if not self._path.exists():\n            return results\n\n        with self._lock:\n            try:\n                with open(self._path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                    for line_num, line in enumerate(f, 1):\n                        try:\n                            data = json.loads(line)\n                            # Convert ISO 8601 string back to datetime object\n                            timestamp_str = data.get(\"timestamp\")\n                            timestamp = datetime.fromisoformat(timestamp_str.replace('Z', '+00:00')) if timestamp_str else datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n                            \n                            results.append(DigitCountResult(\n                                input_value=data[\"input\"],\n                                even=data[\"even\"],\n                                odd=data[\"odd\"],\n                                timestamp=timestamp\n                            ))\n                        except (json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError) as e:\n                            logger.warning(f\"Skipping malformed or incomplete JSON line {line_num} in {self._path}: {e}\")\n            except IOError as e:\n                logger.error(f\"Failed to read history records from {self._path}: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n        return results\n\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/controllers/__init__.py\n# Marker file for Python package\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/controllers/cli.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom digitstats.models import DigitCountResult\nfrom digitstats.services.counter import EvenOddCounter\nfrom digitstats.repositories.history_repo import HistoryRepository, JSONFileHistoryRepository\nfrom digitstats.exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom digitstats.utils.logger import logger\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line interface operations for digit counting.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, counter: EvenOddCounter | None = None, repo: HistoryRepository | None = None):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLI controller with optional counter and repository instances.\"\"\"\n        self.counter = counter or EvenOddCounter()\n        self.repo = repo # Will be explicitly set in cli_entry or re-initialized if history-file is set.\n\n    def run(self, argv: list[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses command-line arguments and executes the requested operation.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for failure).\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"digitstats\",\n            description=\"Count even and odd digits in a number.\"\n        )\n        \n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True, help=\"Available commands\")\n\n        # 'count' command parser\n        count_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n            \"count\",\n            help=\"Count even and odd digits in a specified number.\"\n        )\n        count_parser.add_argument(\n            \"number\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"The integer or numeric string to count digits from (e.g., 123, -45, '007').\"\n        )\n        count_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--json\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Output result in JSON format.\"\n        )\n        count_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--no-persist\",\n            action=\"store_true\",\n            help=\"Do not persist the invocation history for this run.\"\n        )\n        count_parser.add_argument(\n            \"--history-file\",\n            type=str,\n            default=JSONFileHistoryRepository.DEFAULT_HISTORY_PATH,\n            help=f\"Specify a custom history file path (default: {JSONFileHistoryRepository.DEFAULT_HISTORY_PATH}).\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        if args.command == \"count\":\n            return self._handle_count_command(args)\n        \n        return 1 # Should not be reached, argparse.required=True ensures command is given\n\n    def _handle_count_command(self, args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Handles the 'count' CLI command.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            # If a custom history file is specified, ensure the repository uses it.\n            # This logic assumes self.repo is initially a JSONFileHistoryRepository from cli_entry.\n            if isinstance(self.repo, JSONFileHistoryRepository) and str(self.repo._path) != str(Path(args.history_file).resolve()):\n                logger.debug(f\"Re-initializing history repository to {args.history_file}\")\n                self.repo = JSONFileHistoryRepository(Path(args.history_file))\n\n            result = self.counter.count(args.number)\n            \n            if not args.no_persist:\n                try:\n                    self.repo.append(result)\n                except Exception as e:\n                    logger.error(f\"CLI persistence failed for input {args.number}: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            \n            self._print_result(result, args.json)\n            return 0 # Success\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            logger.error(f\"Error: Invalid input provided: {e}\")\n            print(f\"Error: Invalid input provided: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Invalid input exit code\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(f\"An unexpected error occurred during CLI command 'count' for input {args.number}.\")\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # General error exit code\n\n    def _print_result(self, result: DigitCountResult, json_output: bool) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Prints the result to stdout in the specified format.\"\"\"\n        if json_output:\n            print(json.dumps(result.to_dict(), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n        else:\n            print(f\"({result.even}, {result.odd})\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/controllers/http_controller.py\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException\nfrom digitstats.schemas.api_schemas import CountRequest, CountResponse\nfrom digitstats.services.counter import EvenOddCounter\nfrom digitstats.repositories.history_repo import HistoryRepository\nfrom digitstats.exceptions import InvalidInputError\nfrom digitstats.utils.logger import logger\n\nclass HTTPController:\n    \"\"\"Handles HTTP requests for digit counting and delegates to services.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, counter: EvenOddCounter, repo: HistoryRepository):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the HTTPController with a counter and history repository.\"\"\"\n        self.counter = counter\n        self.repo = repo\n\n    async def post_count(self, req: CountRequest) -> CountResponse:\n        \"\"\"\n        Processes a POST request to count even and odd digits.\n        Persists the result and returns a structured JSON response.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            result = self.counter.count(req.number)\n            try:\n                # Persistence is synchronous in this design.\n                self.repo.append(result)\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Log persistence failure but do not prevent returning the result\n                logger.error(f\"HTTP API persistence failed for input {req.number}: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n            \n            return CountResponse(input=result.input_value, even=result.even, odd=result.odd, timestamp=result.timestamp)\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            logger.warning(f\"Bad Request for input {req.number}: {e}\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=f\"Invalid input: {e}\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.exception(f\"Internal server error processing input {req.number}.\")\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\"Internal server error\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/adapters/__init__.py\n# Marker file for Python package\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/adapters/http_app.py\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom digitstats.services.counter import EvenOddCounter\nfrom digitstats.repositories.history_repo import JSONFileHistoryRepository, HistoryRepository\nfrom digitstats.controllers.http_controller import HTTPController\nfrom digitstats.schemas.api_schemas import CountRequest, CountResponse\nfrom digitstats.utils.logger import logger\n\nclass FastAPIAppFactory:\n    \"\"\"Factory for creating and configuring the FastAPI application.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def create_app(repo: HistoryRepository | None = None) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"\n        Creates and configures a FastAPI application instance.\n        Dependencies (EvenOddCounter, HistoryRepository) are wired here.\n        \"\"\"\n        logger.info(\"Creating FastAPI application...\")\n        \n        # Dependency Injection\n        history_repo = repo or JSONFileHistoryRepository()\n        even_odd_counter = EvenOddCounter()\n        http_controller = HTTPController(even_odd_counter, history_repo)\n\n        app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"DigitStats API\",\n            description=\"API to count even and odd digits in numbers.\",\n            version=\"0.1.0\",\n        )\n\n        # Register routes\n        @app.post(\"/count\", response_model=CountResponse, summary=\"Count even and odd digits\")\n        async def count_endpoint(payload: CountRequest):\n            \"\"\"\n            Accepts an integer or numeric string and returns the counts of even and odd digits.\n            \"\"\"\n            return await http_controller.post_count(payload)\n\n        logger.info(\"FastAPI application created and routes registered.\")\n        return app\n\n# The uvicorn entry point typically looks for an 'app' instance.\n# We create it directly for simplicity as per common FastAPI patterns.\n# Also configure logging for the HTTP server instance.\nlogger.info(\"Configuring logger for HTTP application.\")\napp = FastAPIAppFactory.create_app()\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/schemas/__init__.py\n# Marker file for Python package\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/schemas/api_schemas.py\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nclass CountRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Pydantic model for the POST /count request body.\"\"\"\n    number: int | str = Field(..., description=\"The integer or numeric string to count digits from.\")\n\nclass CountResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Pydantic model for the POST /count response body.\"\"\"\n    # Note: 'input' here maps to DigitCountResult.input_value which is an int.\n    # The original input (int|str) is parsed and stored as int in the domain model.\n    input: int = Field(..., description=\"The original input value as an integer.\")\n    even: int = Field(..., description=\"The count of even digits.\")\n    odd: int = Field(..., description=\"The count of odd digits.\")\n    timestamp: datetime = Field(..., description=\"Timestamp of when the count was performed (ISO 8601 UTC).\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/utils/__init__.py\n# Marker file for Python package\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/utils/logger.py\nimport logging\nimport sys\n\nclass LoggerConfig:\n    \"\"\"Configures the application-wide logger.\"\"\"\n\n    _logger_instance: logging.Logger | None = None\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def configure(level: str = \"INFO\") -> logging.Logger:\n        \"\"\"Sets up a basic logger with a console handler.\"\"\"\n        if LoggerConfig._logger_instance is None:\n            log_level = getattr(logging, level.upper(), logging.INFO)\n            logging.basicConfig(\n                level=log_level,\n                format=\"%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s\",\n                handlers=[\n                    logging.StreamHandler(sys.stdout)\n                ]\n            )\n            LoggerConfig._logger_instance = logging.getLogger(\"digitstats\")\n        return LoggerConfig._logger_instance\n\n# Global logger instance for easy import\nlogger = LoggerConfig.configure()\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/exceptions.py\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised for invalid input formats.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n```python\n# src/digitstats/cli_entry.py\nimport sys\nfrom digitstats.controllers.cli import CLIController\nfrom digitstats.repositories.history_repo import JSONFileHistoryRepository\nfrom digitstats.services.counter import EvenOddCounter\nfrom digitstats.utils.logger import LoggerConfig\n\ndef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Entry point for the command-line interface.\n    Configures logging, initializes dependencies, and runs the CLI controller.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Configure logger first\n    # For CLI, INFO level is usually sufficient for user feedback.\n    # Level can be customized via environment variables or CLI flags if needed.\n    LoggerConfig.configure(level=\"INFO\") \n    \n    # Initialize core components\n    history_repo = JSONFileHistoryRepository()\n    even_odd_counter = EvenOddCounter()\n    \n    # Instantiate CLI controller with dependencies\n    controller = CLIController(counter=even_odd_counter, repo=history_repo)\n    \n    # Run the CLI\n    return controller.run(argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n\n```\n```python\n# tests/__init__.py\n# Marker file for Python package\n```\n```python\n# tests/test_counter.py\nimport pytest\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom digitstats.services.counter import EvenOddCounter\nfrom digitstats.services.validator import InputValidator\nfrom digitstats.models import DigitCountResult\nfrom digitstats.exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef counter():\n    \"\"\"Provides a fresh EvenOddCounter instance for each test.\"\"\"\n    return EvenOddCounter(validator=InputValidator())\n\ndef test_even_odd_basic(counter):\n    \"\"\"Tests basic counting with a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    result = counter.count(123)\n    assert result.input_value == 123\n    assert result.even == 1 # '2'\n    assert result.odd == 2 # '1', '3'\n    assert isinstance(result, DigitCountResult)\n    assert isinstance(result.timestamp, datetime)\n\ndef test_negative_number(counter):\n    \"\"\"Tests counting with a negative integer, sign should be ignored for counting.\"\"\"\n    result = counter.count(-12)\n    assert result.input_value == -12\n    assert result.even == 1 # '2'\n    assert result.odd == 1 # '1'\n\ndef test_zero(counter):\n    \"\"\"Tests counting with zero.\"\"\"\n    result = counter.count(0)\n    assert result.input_value == 0\n    assert result.even == 1 # '0'\n    assert result.odd == 0\n\ndef test_large_number(counter):\n    \"\"\"Tests counting with a large number.\"\"\"\n    result = counter.count(1234567890)\n    assert result.input_value == 1234567890\n    assert result.even == 5 # 2,4,6,8,0\n    assert result.odd == 5 # 1,3,5,7,9\n\ndef test_string_input(counter):\n    \"\"\"Tests counting with a numeric string input.\"\"\"\n    result = counter.count(\"98765\")\n    assert result.input_value == 98765\n    assert result.even == 2 # '8', '6'\n    assert result.odd == 3 # '9', '